{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01EMbfHB9xmraosnRexcd9MG","type":"tool_result","content":[{"type":"text","text":"{"commits":[{"hash":"81c24905675b9e4228681e1d1465497226f8d2d7","date":"2026-09-25T21:10:51+03:00","message":"(BREAKING) Remove offline support from patient management (#2776)","refs":"","body":"","authorName":"Dennis Kigen","authorEmail":"kigen.work@gmail.com"},{"hash":"4ba9eec05bf13614f7911dd1871104c086a032f8","date":"2026-09-23T14:45:05-04:00","message":"(feat) Remove fake patient lists (#2770)","refs":"","body":"* (feat) Remove fake patient lists\n\nFake patient lists were added to support a list of offline patients. With\noffline removed, this is no longer something we need.\n\n* Remove unnecessary comment","authorName":"Ian","authorEmail":"52504170+ibacher@users.noreply.github.com"},{"hash":"5fc0dc3f780ec9c00c40e48e3215b805eca2bc26","date":"2026-05-13T20:23:11+03:00","message":"(chore) Migrate from jest to vitest (#2532)","refs":"","body":"* (chore) Migrate from jest to vitest\n\nSwap the test runner from jest to vitest across all nine workspace\npackages, aligning patient-management with the patterns adopted\nacross the rest of the O3 apps.\n\n- Root: replace jest, @swc/jest, jest-cli, jest-environment-jsdom,\n  and @types/jest with vitest, @vitest/coverage-v8, jsdom, and\n  bumped cross-env (7.x to 10.x). Bump @testing-library/dom (9 to 10),\n  @testing-library/jest-dom (6.1 to 6.8), and @testing-library/react\n  (14 to 16) so the /vitest subpath is available. Delete the root\n  jest.config.js.\n- Add a single root vitest.config.ts shared by all packages. Uses\n  jsdom; aliases .scss/.css to identity-obj-proxy via the anchored\n  ^.*\\.s?css$ regex; uses exact-match regex aliases (e.g.\n  /^@openmrs\\/esm-framework$/) for @openmrs/esm-framework and\n  @openmrs/esm-translations so the alias does not capture the\n  /mock subpath; aliases react-i18next to the local __mocks__ file;\n  exposes the tools and __mocks__ paths the way the jest config did\n  via moduleDirectories; pins uuid to the top-level install so\n  esm-offline's nested uuid wrapper doesn't blow up under ESM; caps\n  fakeTimers.toFake so it does not break React's scheduler. Sets\n  process.env.TZ = 'UTC' so the test scripts can drop cross-env.\n- Update tools/setup-tests.ts to load @testing-library/jest-dom/vitest\n  and swap jest.* for vi.* across the mocks (single-spa,\n  scrollIntoView, matchMedia, ResizeObserver-as-class).\n- Update every package's test scripts to `yarn run -T vitest run\n  --passWithNoTests` etc. The -T flag tells yarn 4 to resolve the\n  binary from the top-level workspace.\n- Convert the 100+ test files to the vitest API: jest.* swapped for\n  vi.*, jest.Mock and jest.SpyInstance type aliases replaced with\n  Mock and MockInstance from vitest. The many vi.mock(path, () =>\n  ({ ...jest.requireActual(path), override })) factories rewritten\n  as the async vi.mock(path, async () => ({ ...((await\n  vi.importActual(path)) as object), override })) form; the `as\n  object` cast keeps eslint's consistent-type-imports rule happy\n  without per-module type imports. Several vi.mock(name, () =>\n  vi.fn()) factories wrapped in { default: vi.fn() } so the\n  factory returns a module object. vi.mock('@openmrs/esm-framework',\n  () => ({ X })) calls in useWardLocation.test.ts and\n  side-menu.test.tsx rewritten as the importOriginal-spreading form\n  so the partial override does not lose the rest of the framework\n  exports.\n- patient-management/packages/esm-ward-app/mock.tsx: this is loaded\n  as a test fixture by ward-view tests, so its inline jest.mock and\n  jest.fn calls are swapped for vi.mock and vi.fn and a top-level\n  `import { vi } from 'vitest'` is added.\n- Replace two `jest.replaceProperty` usages (in ward-view and\n  admit-patient-form tests) with a small local replaceProperty\n  helper, since vitest has no direct equivalent.\n- Rewrite the IntersectionObserver mock in ward-view.test.tsx and\n  the ResizeObserver mock in tools/setup-tests.ts as ES classes;\n  vitest's vi.fn().mockImplementation(...) is not constructable.\n- Add explicit `import { vi, describe, it, expect, ... } from\n  'vitest'` to test files. Where the field.resource mock uses jest.fn\n  outside a test file, also import vi.\n- Rewrite the xit in appointments/appointment-tabs.test.tsx as\n  it.skip; xit is not a vitest global.\n- Skip one pre-existing field.test.tsx case\n  (`should render AddressComponent component when name prop is\n  \"address\"`) that performs vi.mock inside an it() and relied on\n  the implicit jest.fn return; it never set a return value via\n  mockReturnValue so the component crashed. Flagged with TODO for a\n  follow-up.\n\n692 tests pass across 8 packages (2 skipped). All packages green\nunder tsc; eslint clean.\n\n* (chore) Address PR review: drop jest shims, fix watch script, add coverage thresholds\n\n- Delete the nine per-package jest.config.js files that re-exported\n  the root config. The root config was already deleted by the\n  migration, so these were broken entry points.\n- Update packages/esm-appointments-app's test-watch script (it still\n  pointed at jest --watch --config jest.config.js) to use vitest watch.\n  Other packages were already updated; this one slipped through\n  because its key was test-watch rather than test:watch and didn't\n  match the original migration's perl rewrite. Renamed to test:watch\n  for consistency.\n- Port coverage configuration from the deleted jest config to\n  vitest.config.ts: 80% global threshold and the same\n  collectCoverageFrom restriction to **/src/**/*.component.tsx.\n\n* (chore) Use fileURLToPath and document the field.test.tsx skip\n\nTwo follow-ups from review:\n\n- vitest.config.ts relied on new URL(...).pathname for setupFiles and\n  six aliases. On Windows .pathname yields /C:/... which is not a\n  valid filesystem path. Add a fileURLToPath helper and route every\n  URL-based path through it, matching the pattern adopted in\n  openmrs-esm-form-builder.\n- The PR body says the field.test.tsx it.skip is flagged with TODO,\n  but no comment was added. Add one explaining why the test is off.\n\n* (chore) Drop dead @openmrs/esm-framework/src/internal alias\n\nvitest.config.ts aliased @openmrs/esm-framework/src/internal to\n@openmrs/esm-framework/mock, but no test file in the repo imports\n/src/internal — the alias was copy-pasted from a sibling project\nand never resolved any module here. Remove it.\n\n* (chore) Hoist replaceProperty helper into tools/\n\nward-view.test.tsx and admit-patient-form.test.tsx each carried a\nbit-identical 8-line replaceProperty helper — the local fill-in for\njest.replaceProperty, which vitest does not implement directly.\n\nMove the helper into tools/test-utils.tsx and export it from tools/,\nalongside the other shared test utilities. Both call sites now import\nit from 'tools' like they do for renderWithSwr.\n\nThe helper's behavior is unchanged: it swaps a writable own property\nand returns a {restore()} handle. The body adds a comment noting it\ndoes not handle getter or non-writable descriptors, which jest's\nreplaceProperty does — neither caller relies on that path.\n\n* (chore) Make each app have independently runnable vitest tests\n\nMirrors the pattern Ian introduced for openmrs-esm-patient-chart in\nPR #3301: a single shared vitest config in tools/, a thin re-export at\nthe workspace root, and a thin merge shim per app. With this in place,\n'cd packages/<app> && yarn test' works without bouncing through the\nworkspace root.\n\n- tools/vitest.shared.ts: the actual config that used to live at\n  vitest.config.ts, with the alias and setupFiles paths rebased from\n  './tools/...' and './__mocks__/...' to './...' and '../__mocks__/...'\n  respectively (it now lives one directory deeper).\n- vitest.config.ts: collapsed to 're-export the shared config' so\n  running 'vitest' at the repo root keeps working.\n- packages/*/vitest.config.ts: nine new thin shims, one per app, that\n  do mergeConfig(sharedConfig, {}). Each app now has a discoverable\n  config when vitest is run from inside the app directory.\n- packages/*/package.json: drop the '-T' flag from the test scripts\n  ('yarn run -T vitest run --passWithNoTests' -> 'vitest run\n  --passWithNoTests'); add 'vitest' as a per-app devDependency so the\n  binary resolves under yarn 4 without the workspace-root hop.\n\n692 tests pass across the 8 packages that have tests (esm-home-app has\nnone); 2 skips unchanged.","authorName":"Dennis Kigen","authorEmail":"kigen.work@gmail.com"},{"hash":"937786ff04595d65324b0ab57e9ad322929d44e6","date":"2025-11-17T14:45:32+05:30","message":"(fix) Fix translation extraction gaps and add missing keys (#2108)","refs":"","body":"- Rename files to canonical naming conventions:\n  - api-remote.ts → patient-list.resource.ts\n  - index.tsx files → descriptive *.component.tsx/*.extension.tsx\n  - before-save-prompt.tsx → before-save-prompt.component.tsx\n  - patient-appointments-header.tsx → patient-appointments-header.component.tsx\n\n- Update extract-translations patterns to include:\n  - *.extension.tsx files (esm-ward-app)\n  - *.resource.ts files (esm-patient-list-management-app)\n\n- Add missing English translation keys:\n  - offlinePatients, unknownError (patient-list-management)\n  - discardModalBody (patient-registration)\n  - close (patient-search)\n  - addPatientToWard, Patient, PatientNote, pendingAdmissions (ward)\n\nEnsures all user-facing strings are captured by extract-translations for Transifex.\n\nCo-authored-by: Dennis Kigen <kigen.work@gmail.com>","authorName":"Nethmi Rodrigo","authorEmail":"nethmi@openmrs.org"},{"hash":"197628dd7756f2f47c76759151e282d1e748840c","date":"2024-01-08T13:14:41Z","message":"(fix) Disable Address Hierarchy for offline patient registration (#910)","refs":"","body":"","authorName":"Jose Francisco","authorEmail":"94977371+icrc-jofrancisco@users.noreply.github.com"},{"hash":"5735345049e958e1d696fecae4c377cf97dafb99","date":"2023-10-02T15:18:22+01:00","message":"(fix) Improve Patient Registration and Offline Functionality (#814)","refs":"","body":"","authorName":"Jose Francisco","authorEmail":"94977371+icrc-jofrancisco@users.noreply.github.com"},{"hash":"541a7fb0fdbdb6bc5c8590b9e0a0d2d26110bb29","date":"2023-06-29T14:38:18+05:30","message":"Fixed the incorrect assignment to isOffline (#746)","refs":"","body":"","authorName":"Vineet Sharma","authorEmail":"sharmava05@gmail.com"},{"hash":"c20d82d7b13de09aedbf057baa868f83e3f391d3","date":"2022-07-14T19:33:37+02:00","message":"Address visual issues with offline patient editing. (#266)","refs":"","body":"","authorName":"Manuel Römer","authorEmail":"30902964+manuelroemer@users.noreply.github.com"},{"hash":"979939a2684c54c457b6c6643038f2edf6183ead","date":"2022-07-06T16:05:57+02:00","message":"(feat) Offline Patient Search (#263)","refs":"","body":"* First iteration of offline patient search for the compact search update.\r\n\r\n* Finalize offline patient search.\r\n\r\n* Update yarn.lock.","authorName":"Manu Römer","authorEmail":"30902964+manuelroemer@users.noreply.github.com"},{"hash":"77f33a5f1a5e01c33037e6f2575088880753d2c0","date":"2022-06-21T15:56:57+02:00","message":"(feat) Offline patient migration to esm-core (#230)","refs":"","body":"* Finalize patient management migration.\r\n\r\n* Translations\r\n\r\n* Migrate to newer sync handlers.\r\n\r\n* Don't fail showing patient lists in the modal dialog when the cohort backend module is not installed.\r\n\r\n* Translations.\r\n\r\n* Improve patient sync handlers.\r\n\r\n* Upgrade package lock.\r\n\r\n* React types resolution.\r\n\r\n* Removed commented out code.","authorName":"Manu Römer","authorEmail":"30902964+manuelroemer@users.noreply.github.com"},{"hash":"20197cc6d17d5166a869a24f08d1303fcd381b9e","date":"2022-04-26T13:02:47+02:00","message":"(feat) Display offline registered patients in offline patients table (#182)","refs":"","body":"* Integrate offline registered patients into the offline patients table.\r\n\r\n* Translations.\r\n\r\n* Allow removing newly registered sync items from the offline patient table.\r\n\r\n* Mutate all SWRs.\r\n\r\n* Fix build by extending dayjs with isToday.","authorName":"Manu Römer","authorEmail":"30902964+manuelroemer@users.noreply.github.com"},{"hash":"c8c6c34f592558bcdb87d4fdf1206a3a58b9cf4b","date":"2022-02-17T11:00:07+01:00","message":"(feat): O3-1111: Allow accessing an offline registered patient's patient registration form from the offline actions table (#113)","refs":"","body":"* Provide interaction between offline actions and editing offline registered patients.\r\n\r\n* Translations.","authorName":"Manu Römer","authorEmail":"30902964+manuelroemer@users.noreply.github.com"},{"hash":"a5e08dd57b2f739cf6dfa425d3ad67f799cbeaf7","date":"2022-02-11T16:56:23+01:00","message":"fix: O3-1092: Show Offline Patient Lists Even If Cohort Lists Fail to Load | Small Cleanup of esm-patient-list-app (#105)","refs":"","body":"* Replaced useAsync/useAsyncQuery with SWR.\r\nRemoved the single `api/index.ts` file in favor of direct imports.\r\n\r\n* Translations.\r\n\r\n* Removed deprecated global-store. (This was long ago migrated to esm-core).\r\n\r\n* Improved naming of hooks.\r\n\r\n* Renamed `queries.ts` to `hooks.ts`.\r\n\r\n* Don't fail displaying the patient lists if one of the two sources cannot load data.","authorName":"Manu Römer","authorEmail":"30902964+manuelroemer@users.noreply.github.com"},{"hash":"d99965c9b1f5d24ac10750f975932eed02a481ee","date":"2022-02-11T12:11:31+01:00","message":"feat: O3-946: Disable unique manually entered patient identifiers in offline mode (#93)","refs":"","body":"* Disable adding/editing unique manual patient identifiers in offline mode.\r\n\r\n* Consider patient identifier lists.\r\n\r\n* Fixed naming.\r\n\r\n* Extract duplicate code.\r\n\r\n* Fixed issues where auto generation option objects could be undefined.\r\n\r\n* PR review. Improved handling of uniquenessBehavior.","authorName":"Manu Römer","authorEmail":"30902964+manuelroemer@users.noreply.github.com"},{"hash":"9f6c60848662c8d8491cfc5cb8d85e5b35a531ba","date":"2022-01-27T11:42:51+01:00","message":"Offline Patient Registration: Interaction Support for Offline Registered Patients | Alignments and Fixes (#86)","refs":"","body":"* Pre-merge master.\r\n\r\n* Provide finalized patient info in sync queue.\r\n\r\n* Translations.\r\n\r\n* Revert package.json.\r\n\r\n* Revert isOffline introduction.\r\n\r\n* Leverage static patient UUIDs during creation.\r\n\r\n* Moved FHIR mapping into control of patient-registration.\r\n\r\n* Improve structure of patient registration sync item. Improve typings.\r\n\r\n* @jsenv/file-size-impact\r\n\r\n* Adapt code style.","authorName":"Manu Römer","authorEmail":"30902964+manuelroemer@users.noreply.github.com"},{"hash":"ffa58e5e34c8801317f82c5625299b310aa3b087","date":"2021-10-07T12:52:01+02:00","message":"Offline Patients: Delete Confirmation Modal | Better Offline Sync API Integration (#50)","refs":"","body":"* Integrated confirmation modal.\r\n\r\n* Integrate new sync item API.\r\n\r\n* Updated deps.\r\n\r\n* Update translations.","authorName":"Manu Römer","authorEmail":"30902964+manuelroemer@users.noreply.github.com"},{"hash":"55780c7320192d114e023bd46eca52f6bd3e96b2","date":"2021-08-31T15:13:51+02:00","message":"Offline Tools Integration: Offline Patients Table (#41)","refs":"","body":"* Added offline patient list table extensions for offline tools.\r\nDeprecated patient list synchronization API.\r\n\r\n* Translation files.\r\n\r\n* Reinstall packages to catch the newest esm-framework APIs.\r\n\r\n* Fixed imports from carbon-components-react.","authorName":"Manu Römer","authorEmail":"30902964+manuelroemer@users.noreply.github.com"},{"hash":"85899c2647147dbdb0fc77377f0e422ac0c7e75d","date":"2021-08-11T22:04:58+02:00","message":"MF-549: Patient Registration: Offline Patient List Integration (#38)","refs":"","body":"* Fixed issue where metadata entries had to exist for an offline list to be interactive.\r\n\r\n* Temp commit.\r\n\r\n* - Create the global store during module setup (consistent with other usages).\r\n- Pluralized \"Patient List\" strings.\r\n\r\n* Localization.\r\n\r\n* Line endings.","authorName":"Manu Römer","authorEmail":"30902964+manuelroemer@users.noreply.github.com"},{"hash":"73a9f1fbe7b2016feceed66d3640664449c44495","date":"2021-08-05T14:33:16+02:00","message":"Fixed issue where metadata entries had to exist for an offline list to be interactive. (#33)","refs":"","body":"","authorName":"Manuel Römer","authorEmail":"30902964+manuelroemer@users.noreply.github.com"},{"hash":"58845482fa46eb1a1a72319a24a6c73a37558100","date":"2021-08-03T18:22:16+02:00","message":"Full Integration of Local Patient Lists Into Current Feature Set | Patient List Project Refactoring & Cleanup (#30)","refs":"","body":"* Generally improved UI responsiveness and user feedback to interactions with the following changes:\r\n\r\n- Added useAsync hook in favor of copy&pasted fetch state handling.\r\n- Moved patient list data fetching and mutating over to useAsync hook.\r\n- Code design: Removed any React.xxx calls in favor of explicit imports (inside patient-list).\r\n\r\n* Restructed API calls in preparation for additional local API functions.\r\n\r\n* Allow adding patients to local and remote patient lists.\r\n\r\n* Do not display local patient lists in the \"Add Patient to List\" modal when the patient is already on that list.\r\n\r\n* Typing updates and finalized migration to query hooks.\r\n\r\n* Refactoring: Made project structure consistent.\r\n\r\n* Reworked global offline patient list change handler store.\r\n\r\n* Rename DB according to naming scheme.\r\n\r\n* import fixup.","authorName":"Manuel Römer","authorEmail":"30902964+manuelroemer@users.noreply.github.com"},{"hash":"f7cd59746f0cb4cd64d2723671d38fdbd8b52455","date":"2021-07-23T22:03:57+02:00","message":"Basic Integration of Offline Patient List into the Patient List Table (#25)","refs":"","body":"* Improved types, added offline patient list.\r\n\r\n* casing\r\n\r\n* Casing\r\n\r\n* Integrated local patient list fetching into hooks.\r\nMigrated fetched data from cohorts to internal PatientList type.\r\n\r\n* Adapt DB name to conventions.\r\n\r\n* Fetch stored metadata of local patient lists from DB.\r\n\r\n* Added function for locally updating patient list.\r\n\r\n* Simple update integration into table.\r\n\r\n* Remove isDeviceLocal flag.\r\n\r\n* Fixed undefined values.\r\n\r\n* Renamed enum to use PascalCase.\r\n\r\n* Improved/Support filtering in general/for local lists.\r\n\r\n* Prettier.","authorName":"Manuel Römer","authorEmail":"30902964+manuelroemer@users.noreply.github.com"},{"hash":"e830ad14d81650cd9eee59f7afabbb45858664a4","date":"2021-07-20T13:01:43+02:00","message":"Deploy patient list (#23)","refs":"","body":"* add offline patient list data\r\n\r\n* review improvements\r\n\r\n* add patient list api, add patient list action button to patient chart\r\n\r\n* remove console.log\r\n\r\n* add modal for adding patients to lists\r\n\r\n* Design completed\r\n\r\n* start replacing the mock with the API\r\n\r\n* Searching patient lists added\r\n\r\n* replace mock with API in hooks\r\n\r\n* Change in structure of PatientListData\r\n\r\n* Selecting and adding patient to list implemented\r\n\r\n* MF-641: Add Patient List Modal (#18)\r\n\r\n* Design completed\r\n\r\n* Searching patient lists added\r\n\r\n* Change in structure of PatientListData\r\n\r\n* Selecting and adding patient to list implemented\r\n\r\n* fix addPatient, add function to retrieve lists for a patient\r\n\r\n* fix API\r\n\r\n* fix getPatientListsForPatient method\r\n\r\n* update yarn.lock\r\n\r\n* Review changes\r\n\r\n* Implemented search\r\n\r\n* Hiding the already enrolled lists completed\r\n\r\nCo-authored-by: Nikita Malyschkin <nikita.malyschkin@googlemail.com>\r\nCo-authored-by: Vineet Sharma <sharmava05@gmail.com>\r\nCo-authored-by: Vineet Sharma <51502471+vasharma05@users.noreply.github.com>","authorName":"Florian Rappl","authorEmail":"rappl.florian@gmail.com"},{"hash":"a9b6d3143b2b5ab975528db4d149fc3157edf390","date":"2021-07-16T23:15:56+02:00","message":"Deploy patient list (#19)","refs":"","body":"* add offline patient list data\r\n\r\n* review improvements\r\n\r\n* add patient list api, add patient list action button to patient chart\r\n\r\n* remove console.log\r\n\r\n* add modal for adding patients to lists\r\n\r\n* start replacing the mock with the API\r\n\r\n* replace mock with API in hooks\r\n\r\n* MF-641: Add Patient List Modal (#18)\r\n\r\n* Design completed\r\n\r\n* Searching patient lists added\r\n\r\n* Change in structure of PatientListData\r\n\r\n* Selecting and adding patient to list implemented\r\n\r\n* fix addPatient, add function to retrieve lists for a patient\r\n\r\n* fix API\r\n\r\n* fix getPatientListsForPatient method\r\n\r\n* update yarn.lock\r\n\r\n* incorperate review feedback\r\n\r\nCo-authored-by: Vineet Sharma <51502471+vasharma05@users.noreply.github.com>","authorName":"Nikita Malyschkin","authorEmail":"44928856+nmalyschkin@users.noreply.github.com"},{"hash":"68d465b9b53798a7d9a14fe62338b9349853b7f1","date":"2021-05-31T13:48:28+02:00","message":"Merge pull request #5 from manuelroemer/feature/offline-editing","refs":"","body":"Offline Patient Editing","authorName":"Florian Rappl","authorEmail":"rappl.florian@gmail.com"},{"hash":"78f1d898249b7d25cd041364886c93bd8cba0946","date":"2021-05-27T15:36:30+02:00","message":"First support for editing queued offline-created patients.","refs":"","body":"","authorName":"Manuel Römer","authorEmail":"30902964+manuelroemer@users.noreply.github.com"},{"hash":"217d31de8491b3fe66cbe6ef08b303b77086211f","date":"2021-05-27T12:27:03+02:00","message":"Fixed patient form editing not working. Added first fns for offline editing.","refs":"","body":"","authorName":"Manuel Römer","authorEmail":"30902964+manuelroemer@users.noreply.github.com"}],"totalCount":26}"}]}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"bfb465e4-c8b2-4b61-a545-94b7863839b7","uuid":"b7b8880a-12bb-440b-869e-ccd74c325d56","timestamp":"2026-10-23T18:04:45.216Z","tool_use_result":[{"type":"text","text":"{"commits":[{"hash":"81c24905675b9e4228681e1d1465497226f8d2d7","date":"2026-09-25T21:10:51+03:00","message":"(BREAKING) Remove offline support from patient management (#2776)","refs":"","body":"","authorName":"Dennis Kigen","authorEmail":"kigen.work@gmail.com"},{"hash":"4ba9eec05bf13614f7911dd1871104c086a032f8","date":"2026-09-23T14:45:05-04:00","message":"(feat) Remove fake patient lists (#2770)","refs":"","body":"* (feat) Remove fake patient lists\n\nFake patient lists were added to support a list of offline patients. With\noffline removed, this is no longer something we need.\n\n* Remove unnecessary comment","authorName":"Ian","authorEmail":"52504170+ibacher@users.noreply.github.com"},{"hash":"5fc0dc3f780ec9c00c40e48e3215b805eca2bc26","date":"2026-05-13T20:23:11+03:00","message":"(chore) Migrate from jest to vitest (#2532)","refs":"","body":"* (chore) Migrate from jest to vitest\n\nSwap the test runner from jest to vitest across all nine workspace\npackages, aligning patient-management with the patterns adopted\nacross the rest of the O3 apps.\n\n- Root: replace jest, @swc/jest, jest-cli, jest-environment-jsdom,\n  and @types/jest with vitest, @vitest/coverage-v8, jsdom, and\n  bumped cross-env (7.x to 10.x). Bump @testing-library/dom (9 to 10),\n  @testing-library/jest-dom (6.1 to 6.8), and @testing-library/react\n  (14 to 16) so the /vitest subpath is available. Delete the root\n  jest.config.js.\n- Add a single root vitest.config.ts shared by all packages. Uses\n  jsdom; aliases .scss/.css to identity-obj-proxy via the anchored\n  ^.*\\.s?css$ regex; uses exact-match regex aliases (e.g.\n  /^@openmrs\\/esm-framework$/) for @openmrs/esm-framework and\n  @openmrs/esm-translations so the alias does not capture the\n  /mock subpath; aliases react-i18next to the local __mocks__ file;\n  exposes the tools and __mocks__ paths the way the jest config did\n  via moduleDirectories; pins uuid to the top-level install so\n  esm-offline's nested uuid wrapper doesn't blow up under ESM; caps\n  fakeTimers.toFake so it does not break React's scheduler. Sets\n  process.env.TZ = 'UTC' so the test scripts can drop cross-env.\n- Update tools/setup-tests.ts to load @testing-library/jest-dom/vitest\n  and swap jest.* for vi.* across the mocks (single-spa,\n  scrollIntoView, matchMedia, ResizeObserver-as-class).\n- Update every package's test scripts to `yarn run -T vitest run\n  --passWithNoTests` etc. The -T flag tells yarn 4 to resolve the\n  binary from the top-level workspace.\n- Convert the 100+ test files to the vitest API: jest.* swapped for\n  vi.*, jest.Mock and jest.SpyInstance type aliases replaced with\n  Mock and MockInstance from vitest. The many vi.mock(path, () =>\n  ({ ...jest.requireActual(path), override })) factories rewritten\n  as the async vi.mock(path, async () => ({ ...((await\n  vi.importActual(path)) as object), override })) form; the `as\n  object` cast keeps eslint's consistent-type-imports rule happy\n  without per-module type imports. Several vi.mock(name, () =>\n  vi.fn()) factories wrapped in { default: vi.fn() } so the\n  factory returns a module object. vi.mock('@openmrs/esm-framework',\n  () => ({ X })) calls in useWardLocation.test.ts and\n  side-menu.test.tsx rewritten as the importOriginal-spreading form\n  so the partial override does not lose the rest of the framework\n  exports.\n- patient-management/packages/esm-ward-app/mock.tsx: this is loaded\n  as a test fixture by ward-view tests, so its inline jest.mock and\n  jest.fn calls are swapped for vi.mock and vi.fn and a top-level\n  `import { vi } from 'vitest'` is added.\n- Replace two `jest.replaceProperty` usages (in ward-view and\n  admit-patient-form tests) with a small local replaceProperty\n  helper, since vitest has no direct equivalent.\n- Rewrite the IntersectionObserver mock in ward-view.test.tsx and\n  the ResizeObserver mock in tools/setup-tests.ts as ES classes;\n  vitest's vi.fn().mockImplementation(...) is not constructable.\n- Add explicit `import { vi, describe, it, expect, ... } from\n  'vitest'` to test files. Where the field.resource mock uses jest.fn\n  outside a test file, also import vi.\n- Rewrite the xit in appointments/appointment-tabs.test.tsx as\n  it.skip; xit is not a vitest global.\n- Skip one pre-existing field.test.tsx case\n  (`should render AddressComponent component when name prop is\n  \"address\"`) that performs vi.mock inside an it() and relied on\n  the implicit jest.fn return; it never set a return value via\n  mockReturnValue so the component crashed. Flagged with TODO for a\n  follow-up.\n\n692 tests pass across 8 packages (2 skipped). All packages green\nunder tsc; eslint clean.\n\n* (chore) Address PR review: drop jest shims, fix watch script, add coverage thresholds\n\n- Delete the nine per-package jest.config.js files that re-exported\n  the root config. The root config was already deleted by the\n  migration, so these were broken entry points.\n- Update packages/esm-appointments-app's test-watch script (it still\n  pointed at jest --watch --config jest.config.js) to use vitest watch.\n  Other packages were already updated; this one slipped through\n  because its key was test-watch rather than test:watch and didn't\n  match the original migration's perl rewrite. Renamed to test:watch\n  for consistency.\n- Port coverage configuration from the deleted jest config to\n  vitest.config.ts: 80% global threshold and the same\n  collectCoverageFrom restriction to **/src/**/*.component.tsx.\n\n* (chore) Use fileURLToPath and document the field.test.tsx skip\n\nTwo follow-ups from review:\n\n- vitest.config.ts relied on new URL(...).pathname for setupFiles and\n  six aliases. On Windows .pathname yields /C:/... which is not a\n  valid filesystem path. Add a fileURLToPath helper and route every\n  URL-based path through it, matching the pattern adopted in\n  openmrs-esm-form-builder.\n- The PR body says the field.test.tsx it.skip is flagged with TODO,\n  but no comment was added. Add one explaining why the test is off.\n\n* (chore) Drop dead @openmrs/esm-framework/src/internal alias\n\nvitest.config.ts aliased @openmrs/esm-framework/src/internal to\n@openmrs/esm-framework/mock, but no test file in the repo imports\n/src/internal — the alias was copy-pasted from a sibling project\nand never resolved any module here. Remove it.\n\n* (chore) Hoist replaceProperty helper into tools/\n\nward-view.test.tsx and admit-patient-form.test.tsx each carried a\nbit-identical 8-line replaceProperty helper — the local fill-in for\njest.replaceProperty, which vitest does not implement directly.\n\nMove the helper into tools/test-utils.tsx and export it from tools/,\nalongside the other shared test utilities. Both call sites now import\nit from 'tools' like they do for renderWithSwr.\n\nThe helper's behavior is unchanged: it swaps a writable own property\nand returns a {restore()} handle. The body adds a comment noting it\ndoes not handle getter or non-writable descriptors, which jest's\nreplaceProperty does — neither caller relies on that path.\n\n* (chore) Make each app have independently runnable vitest tests\n\nMirrors the pattern Ian introduced for openmrs-esm-patient-chart in\nPR #3301: a single shared vitest config in tools/, a thin re-export at\nthe workspace root, and a thin merge shim per app. With this in place,\n'cd packages/<app> && yarn test' works without bouncing through the\nworkspace root.\n\n- tools/vitest.shared.ts: the actual config that used to live at\n  vitest.config.ts, with the alias and setupFiles paths rebased from\n  './tools/...' and './__mocks__/...' to './...' and '../__mocks__/...'\n  respectively (it now lives one directory deeper).\n- vitest.config.ts: collapsed to 're-export the shared config' so\n  running 'vitest' at the repo root keeps working.\n- packages/*/vitest.config.ts: nine new thin shims, one per app, that\n  do mergeConfig(sharedConfig, {}). Each app now has a discoverable\n  config when vitest is run from inside the app directory.\n- packages/*/package.json: drop the '-T' flag from the test scripts\n  ('yarn run -T vitest run --passWithNoTests' -> 'vitest run\n  --passWithNoTests'); add 'vitest' as a per-app devDependency so the\n  binary resolves under yarn 4 without the workspace-root hop.\n\n692 tests pass across the 8 packages that have tests (esm-home-app has\nnone); 2 skips unchanged.","authorName":"Dennis Kigen","authorEmail":"kigen.work@gmail.com"},{"hash":"937786ff04595d65324b0ab57e9ad322929d44e6","date":"2025-11-17T14:45:32+05:30","message":"(fix) Fix translation extraction gaps and add missing keys (#2108)","refs":"","body":"- Rename files to canonical naming conventions:\n  - api-remote.ts → patient-list.resource.ts\n  - index.tsx files → descriptive *.component.tsx/*.extension.tsx\n  - before-save-prompt.tsx → before-save-prompt.component.tsx\n  - patient-appointments-header.tsx → patient-appointments-header.component.tsx\n\n- Update extract-translations patterns to include:\n  - *.extension.tsx files (esm-ward-app)\n  - *.resource.ts files (esm-patient-list-management-app)\n\n- Add missing English translation keys:\n  - offlinePatients, unknownError (patient-list-management)\n  - discardModalBody (patient-registration)\n  - close (patient-search)\n  - addPatientToWard, Patient, PatientNote, pendingAdmissions (ward)\n\nEnsures all user-facing strings are captured by extract-translations for Transifex.\n\nCo-authored-by: Dennis Kigen <kigen.work@gmail.com>","authorName":"Nethmi Rodrigo","authorEmail":"nethmi@openmrs.org"},{"hash":"197628dd7756f2f47c76759151e282d1e748840c","date":"2024-01-08T13:14:41Z","message":"(fix) Disable Address Hierarchy for offline patient registration (#910)","refs":"","body":"","authorName":"Jose Francisco","authorEmail":"94977371+icrc-jofrancisco@users.noreply.github.com"},{"hash":"5735345049e958e1d696fecae4c377cf97dafb99","date":"2023-10-02T15:18:22+01:00","message":"(fix) Improve Patient Registration and Offline Functionality (#814)","refs":"","body":"","authorName":"Jose Francisco","authorEmail":"94977371+icrc-jofrancisco@users.noreply.github.com"},{"hash":"541a7fb0fdbdb6bc5c8590b9e0a0d2d26110bb29","date":"2023-06-29T14:38:18+05:30","message":"Fixed the incorrect assignment to isOffline (#746)","refs":"","body":"","authorName":"Vineet Sharma","authorEmail":"sharmava05@gmail.com"},{"hash":"c20d82d7b13de09aedbf057baa868f83e3f391d3","date":"2022-07-14T19:33:37+02:00","message":"Address visual issues with offline patient editing. (#266)","refs":"","body":"","authorName":"Manuel Römer","authorEmail":"30902964+manuelroemer@users.noreply.github.com"},{"hash":"979939a2684c54c457b6c6643038f2edf6183ead","date":"2022-07-06T16:05:57+02:00","message":"(feat) Offline Patient Search (#263)","refs":"","body":"* First iteration of offline patient search for the compact search update.\r\n\r\n* Finalize offline patient search.\r\n\r\n* Update yarn.lock.","authorName":"Manu Römer","authorEmail":"30902964+manuelroemer@users.noreply.github.com"},{"hash":"77f33a5f1a5e01c33037e6f2575088880753d2c0","date":"2022-06-21T15:56:57+02:00","message":"(feat) Offline patient migration to esm-core (#230)","refs":"","body":"* Finalize patient management migration.\r\n\r\n* Translations\r\n\r\n* Migrate to newer sync handlers.\r\n\r\n* Don't fail showing patient lists in the modal dialog when the cohort backend module is not installed.\r\n\r\n* Translations.\r\n\r\n* Improve patient sync handlers.\r\n\r\n* Upgrade package lock.\r\n\r\n* React types resolution.\r\n\r\n* Removed commented out code.","authorName":"Manu Römer","authorEmail":"30902964+manuelroemer@users.noreply.github.com"},{"hash":"20197cc6d17d5166a869a24f08d1303fcd381b9e","date":"2022-04-26T13:02:47+02:00","message":"(feat) Display offline registered patients in offline patients table (#182)","refs":"","body":"* Integrate offline registered patients into the offline patients table.\r\n\r\n* Translations.\r\n\r\n* Allow removing newly registered sync items from the offline patient table.\r\n\r\n* Mutate all SWRs.\r\n\r\n* Fix build by extending dayjs with isToday.","authorName":"Manu Römer","authorEmail":"30902964+manuelroemer@users.noreply.github.com"},{"hash":"c8c6c34f592558bcdb87d4fdf1206a3a58b9cf4b","date":"2022-02-17T11:00:07+01:00","message":"(feat): O3-1111: Allow accessing an offline registered patient's patient registration form from the offline actions table (#113)","refs":"","body":"* Provide interaction between offline actions and editing offline registered patients.\r\n\r\n* Translations.","authorName":"Manu Römer","authorEmail":"30902964+manuelroemer@users.noreply.github.com"},{"hash":"a5e08dd57b2f739cf6dfa425d3ad67f799cbeaf7","date":"2022-02-11T16:56:23+01:00","message":"fix: O3-1092: Show Offline Patient Lists Even If Cohort Lists Fail to Load | Small Cleanup of esm-patient-list-app (#105)","refs":"","body":"* Replaced useAsync/useAsyncQuery with SWR.\r\nRemoved the single `api/index.ts` file in favor of direct imports.\r\n\r\n* Translations.\r\n\r\n* Removed deprecated global-store. (This was long ago migrated to esm-core).\r\n\r\n* Improved naming of hooks.\r\n\r\n* Renamed `queries.ts` to `hooks.ts`.\r\n\r\n* Don't fail displaying the patient lists if one of the two sources cannot load data.","authorName":"Manu Römer","authorEmail":"30902964+manuelroemer@users.noreply.github.com"},{"hash":"d99965c9b1f5d24ac10750f975932eed02a481ee","date":"2022-02-11T12:11:31+01:00","message":"feat: O3-946: Disable unique manually entered patient identifiers in offline mode (#93)","refs":"","body":"* Disable adding/editing unique manual patient identifiers in offline mode.\r\n\r\n* Consider patient identifier lists.\r\n\r\n* Fixed naming.\r\n\r\n* Extract duplicate code.\r\n\r\n* Fixed issues where auto generation option objects could be undefined.\r\n\r\n* PR review. Improved handling of uniquenessBehavior.","authorName":"Manu Römer","authorEmail":"30902964+manuelroemer@users.noreply.github.com"},{"hash":"9f6c60848662c8d8491cfc5cb8d85e5b35a531ba","date":"2022-01-27T11:42:51+01:00","message":"Offline Patient Registration: Interaction Support for Offline Registered Patients | Alignments and Fixes (#86)","refs":"","body":"* Pre-merge master.\r\n\r\n* Provide finalized patient info in sync queue.\r\n\r\n* Translations.\r\n\r\n* Revert package.json.\r\n\r\n* Revert isOffline introduction.\r\n\r\n* Leverage static patient UUIDs during creation.\r\n\r\n* Moved FHIR mapping into control of patient-registration.\r\n\r\n* Improve structure of patient registration sync item. Improve typings.\r\n\r\n* @jsenv/file-size-impact\r\n\r\n* Adapt code style.","authorName":"Manu Römer","authorEmail":"30902964+manuelroemer@users.noreply.github.com"},{"hash":"ffa58e5e34c8801317f82c5625299b310aa3b087","date":"2021-10-07T12:52:01+02:00","message":"Offline Patients: Delete Confirmation Modal | Better Offline Sync API Integration (#50)","refs":"","body":"* Integrated confirmation modal.\r\n\r\n* Integrate new sync item API.\r\n\r\n* Updated deps.\r\n\r\n* Update translations.","authorName":"Manu Römer","authorEmail":"30902964+manuelroemer@users.noreply.github.com"},{"hash":"55780c7320192d114e023bd46eca52f6bd3e96b2","date":"2021-08-31T15:13:51+02:00","message":"Offline Tools Integration: Offline Patients Table (#41)","refs":"","body":"* Added offline patient list table extensions for offline tools.\r\nDeprecated patient list synchronization API.\r\n\r\n* Translation files.\r\n\r\n* Reinstall packages to catch the newest esm-framework APIs.\r\n\r\n* Fixed imports from carbon-components-react.","authorName":"Manu Römer","authorEmail":"30902964+manuelroemer@users.noreply.github.com"},{"hash":"85899c2647147dbdb0fc77377f0e422ac0c7e75d","date":"2021-08-11T22:04:58+02:00","message":"MF-549: Patient Registration: Offline Patient List Integration (#38)","refs":"","body":"* Fixed issue where metadata entries had to exist for an offline list to be interactive.\r\n\r\n* Temp commit.\r\n\r\n* - Create the global store during module setup (consistent with other usages).\r\n- Pluralized \"Patient List\" strings.\r\n\r\n* Localization.\r\n\r\n* Line endings.","authorName":"Manu Römer","authorEmail":"30902964+manuelroemer@users.noreply.github.com"},{"hash":"73a9f1fbe7b2016feceed66d3640664449c44495","date":"2021-08-05T14:33:16+02:00","message":"Fixed issue where metadata entries had to exist for an offline list to be interactive. (#33)","refs":"","body":"","authorName":"Manuel Römer","authorEmail":"30902964+manuelroemer@users.noreply.github.com"},{"hash":"58845482fa46eb1a1a72319a24a6c73a37558100","date":"2021-08-03T18:22:16+02:00","message":"Full Integration of Local Patient Lists Into Current Feature Set | Patient List Project Refactoring & Cleanup (#30)","refs":"","body":"* Generally improved UI responsiveness and user feedback to interactions with the following changes:\r\n\r\n- Added useAsync hook in favor of copy&pasted fetch state handling.\r\n- Moved patient list data fetching and mutating over to useAsync hook.\r\n- Code design: Removed any React.xxx calls in favor of explicit imports (inside patient-list).\r\n\r\n* Restructed API calls in preparation for additional local API functions.\r\n\r\n* Allow adding patients to local and remote patient lists.\r\n\r\n* Do not display local patient lists in the \"Add Patient to List\" modal when the patient is already on that list.\r\n\r\n* Typing updates and finalized migration to query hooks.\r\n\r\n* Refactoring: Made project structure consistent.\r\n\r\n* Reworked global offline patient list change handler store.\r\n\r\n* Rename DB according to naming scheme.\r\n\r\n* import fixup.","authorName":"Manuel Römer","authorEmail":"30902964+manuelroemer@users.noreply.github.com"},{"hash":"f7cd59746f0cb4cd64d2723671d38fdbd8b52455","date":"2021-07-23T22:03:57+02:00","message":"Basic Integration of Offline Patient List into the Patient List Table (#25)","refs":"","body":"* Improved types, added offline patient list.\r\n\r\n* casing\r\n\r\n* Casing\r\n\r\n* Integrated local patient list fetching into hooks.\r\nMigrated fetched data from cohorts to internal PatientList type.\r\n\r\n* Adapt DB name to conventions.\r\n\r\n* Fetch stored metadata of local patient lists from DB.\r\n\r\n* Added function for locally updating patient list.\r\n\r\n* Simple update integration into table.\r\n\r\n* Remove isDeviceLocal flag.\r\n\r\n* Fixed undefined values.\r\n\r\n* Renamed enum to use PascalCase.\r\n\r\n* Improved/Support filtering in general/for local lists.\r\n\r\n* Prettier.","authorName":"Manuel Römer","authorEmail":"30902964+manuelroemer@users.noreply.github.com"},{"hash":"e830ad14d81650cd9eee59f7afabbb45858664a4","date":"2021-07-20T13:01:43+02:00","message":"Deploy patient list (#23)","refs":"","body":"* add offline patient list data\r\n\r\n* review improvements\r\n\r\n* add patient list api, add patient list action button to patient chart\r\n\r\n* remove console.log\r\n\r\n* add modal for adding patients to lists\r\n\r\n* Design completed\r\n\r\n* start replacing the mock with the API\r\n\r\n* Searching patient lists added\r\n\r\n* replace mock with API in hooks\r\n\r\n* Change in structure of PatientListData\r\n\r\n* Selecting and adding patient to list implemented\r\n\r\n* MF-641: Add Patient List Modal (#18)\r\n\r\n* Design completed\r\n\r\n* Searching patient lists added\r\n\r\n* Change in structure of PatientListData\r\n\r\n* Selecting and adding patient to list implemented\r\n\r\n* fix addPatient, add function to retrieve lists for a patient\r\n\r\n* fix API\r\n\r\n* fix getPatientListsForPatient method\r\n\r\n* update yarn.lock\r\n\r\n* Review changes\r\n\r\n* Implemented search\r\n\r\n* Hiding the already enrolled lists completed\r\n\r\nCo-authored-by: Nikita Malyschkin <nikita.malyschkin@googlemail.com>\r\nCo-authored-by: Vineet Sharma <sharmava05@gmail.com>\r\nCo-authored-by: Vineet Sharma <51502471+vasharma05@users.noreply.github.com>","authorName":"Florian Rappl","authorEmail":"rappl.florian@gmail.com"},{"hash":"a9b6d3143b2b5ab975528db4d149fc3157edf390","date":"2021-07-16T23:15:56+02:00","message":"Deploy patient list (#19)","refs":"","body":"* add offline patient list data\r\n\r\n* review improvements\r\n\r\n* add patient list api, add patient list action button to patient chart\r\n\r\n* remove console.log\r\n\r\n* add modal for adding patients to lists\r\n\r\n* start replacing the mock with the API\r\n\r\n* replace mock with API in hooks\r\n\r\n* MF-641: Add Patient List Modal (#18)\r\n\r\n* Design completed\r\n\r\n* Searching patient lists added\r\n\r\n* Change in structure of PatientListData\r\n\r\n* Selecting and adding patient to list implemented\r\n\r\n* fix addPatient, add function to retrieve lists for a patient\r\n\r\n* fix API\r\n\r\n* fix getPatientListsForPatient method\r\n\r\n* update yarn.lock\r\n\r\n* incorperate review feedback\r\n\r\nCo-authored-by: Vineet Sharma <51502471+vasharma05@users.noreply.github.com>","authorName":"Nikita Malyschkin","authorEmail":"44928856+nmalyschkin@users.noreply.github.com"},{"hash":"68d465b9b53798a7d9a14fe62338b9349853b7f1","date":"2021-05-31T13:48:28+02:00","message":"Merge pull request #5 from manuelroemer/feature/offline-editing","refs":"","body":"Offline Patient Editing","authorName":"Florian Rappl","authorEmail":"rappl.florian@gmail.com"},{"hash":"78f1d898249b7d25cd041364886c93bd8cba0946","date":"2021-05-27T15:36:30+02:00","message":"First support for editing queued offline-created patients.","refs":"","body":"","authorName":"Manuel Römer","authorEmail":"30902964+manuelroemer@users.noreply.github.com"},{"hash":"217d31de8491b3fe66cbe6ef08b303b77086211f","date":"2021-05-27T12:27:03+02:00","message":"Fixed patient form editing not working. Added first fns for offline editing.","refs":"","body":"","authorName":"Manuel Römer","authorEmail":"30902964+manuelroemer@users.noreply.github.com"}],"totalCount":26}"}],"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_01EMbfHB9xmraosnRexcd9MG","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"rule"}}]}
