{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-haiku-5-5","id":"msg_011CgKcQ1h4RYwALbAKDsbyK","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01WkovkBX5NSMPf8HUfpgnG3","name":"mcp__falkon__list_commits","input":{"repo":"github.com/openmrs/openmrs-esm-core","query":"cache","since":"2025-06-01","perPage":30},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":15707,"cache_read_input_tokens":19777,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":15707},"output_tokens":3,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"bfb465e4-c8b2-4b61-a545-94b7863839b7","uuid":"d0297f3e-e820-4b89-86b6-fe1cc49bb880","timestamp":"2026-10-23T18:04:48.939Z","request_id":"req_011CgKcQ1LiV9fRiKYSo8aCx","wire_tool_inputs":{"toolu_01WkovkBX5NSMPf8HUfpgnG3":{"repo":"github.com/openmrs/openmrs-esm-core","query":"cache","since":"2025-06-01","perPage":30}},"tool_use_meta":[{"id":"toolu_01WkovkBX5NSMPf8HUfpgnG3","display_name":"List Commits","server_display_name":"falkon-mcp-server","tool_name":"list_commits"}]}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01WkovkBX5NSMPf8HUfpgnG3","type":"tool_result","content":[{"type":"text","text":"{"commits":[{"hash":"14197959572c1be0268228ebe25612161a3b6412","date":"2026-09-30T20:02:41+03:00","message":"(fix) Clear the shared SWR cache on logout (#1919)","refs":"","body":"* (fix) Clear the shared SWR cache on logout\n\nLogout called SWR's global `mutate`, which targets SWR's default cache\nrather than the shared cache that `openmrsComponentDecorator` provides to\nO3 apps. Logout navigates to the login page without a reload, so the\nprevious user's cached data survived into the next session in the same\ntab and rendered before revalidating.\n\nRedirectLogout now passes `cache` and `mutate` from `useSWRConfig()` to\n`performLogout`, which clears every cached key by name. Clearing by name\nis needed because a key-filter `mutate(() => true)` skips the\n`useSWRInfinite` and `useSWRSubscription` keys.\n\n* Clear the SWR cache before the early login redirect\n\nlogout() marks the session as logged out before it resolves. That\nre-runs the RedirectLogout effect, which redirects to the login page\nbefore performLogout has cleared the cache. Clear the cache in that\nbranch too, right before redirecting.\n\n* Mark the early cache clear as intentionally unawaited\n\nThe unauthenticated branch starts the SWR cache clear without awaiting\nit, because SWR updates the cache synchronously and the redirect only\nneeds that update. Mark the promise with `void` so it reads as\ndeliberately ignored rather than forgotten.","authorName":"Dennis Kigen","authorEmail":"kigen.work@gmail.com"},{"hash":"7cf6fef6986bc68a6fa55c2f56ec96f399271527","date":"2026-09-28T23:25:32+03:00","message":"(fix) Stop the E2E dependency caches from overwriting each other","refs":"","body":"Scope each node_modules cache in the E2E workflow to its own repo. The\nesm-core caches now exclude e2e_repo/**, and the cache for the checked-out\nrepo only covers e2e_repo/**/node_modules and includes the repo name in its\nkey.\n\nBoth caches used to cache **/node_modules from the workspace root, so each\none matched esm-core's node_modules as well as e2e_repo's. Restoring the\nother repo's cache overwrote esm-core's fresh install with the esm-core\nnode_modules saved alongside it, and the esm-core cache step then saved\nthat mixed tree under esm-core's lockfile key.\n\nAfter the turbo upgrade, the patient-chart cache still held esm-core's\npre-upgrade node_modules. It was restored over the new install and saved\nas main's esm-core cache. Runs that restored that entry skipped yarn\ninstall, and yarn turbo failed with \"Couldn't find a script named turbo\"\nbecause node_modules/.yarn-state.yml still described turbo 2.5.2.\n\ndeploy-pages uses the same path list as the E2E esm-core cache so the two\nkeep sharing entries. Changing the paths also changes the cache version,\nso entries saved with the old paths are no longer restored.\n","authorName":"Dennis Kigen","authorEmail":"kigen.work@gmail.com"},{"hash":"fb886e7a893d1638bb65ea0136967c99029ac54b","date":"2026-09-18T20:22:04+03:00","message":"(feat) O3-5986: Let attachments be recorded on and read by encounter (#1887)","refs":"","body":"* (feat) O3-5986: Let attachments be recorded on and read by encounter\n\ncreateAttachment now takes an optional encounter UUID and sends it as the\n`encounter` form field. That lets the visit note form record an image on the\nnote's own encounter instead of leaving it encounterless, which is why saved\nimages never show up again when we reopen the note.\n\ngetAttachments and useAttachments take the same optional UUID and hit\n`/attachment?patient=...&encounter=...` when it's set. We leave\nincludeEncounterless out of that request on purpose: the attachments module\nignores the encounter filter whenever includeEncounterless is present. Both\ngo through a new getAttachmentsUrl helper so the fetch and the SWR cache key\nare always the same string, and consumers can build that key when they need\nto invalidate it.\n\nExisting callers are unchanged. Adds the first tests for these helpers,\nmirrors the helper in the emr-api and storybook mocks and regenerates the\nAPI docs.\n\n* Skip the attachments fetch while the patient UUID is empty\n\nuseAttachments now passes a null SWR key when patientUuid is falsy, the same\nway usePatient does, so a form can defer the request until it knows which\nencounter to load.\n\n* Warn about unresolvable encounter UUIDs in the attachment docs\n\nThe attachments module resolves the encounter param with getEncounterByUuid\nand, when that yields null with no includeEncounterless flag, falls back to\nevery attachment of the patient. Callers should only pass an encounter UUID\nthey have already loaded.","authorName":"Dennis Kigen","authorEmail":"kigen.work@gmail.com"},{"hash":"92bf2449a4eef5836fbb8abd20fbb6d752633ea6","date":"2026-09-18T12:56:05-04:00","message":"(chore) Switch to using GitHub Actions cache for Actions","refs":"","body":"","authorName":"Ian","authorEmail":"ian.c.bacher@gmail.com"},{"hash":"eef2c97e8feb401ed3f5a5951ceaca1a0418bbe9","date":"2026-08-28T15:47:12-04:00","message":"(fix) Import map and routes should be cached (#1855)","refs":"","body":"Co-authored-by: Dennis Kigen <kigen.work@gmail.com>","authorName":"Ian","authorEmail":"52504170+ibacher@users.noreply.github.com"},{"hash":"8aa137ceb1785269c8c2636ac225f69dcbda3181","date":"2026-08-04T23:19:08+03:00","message":"(feat) Adopt ESLint 9 and the shared @openmrs/eslint-config (#1827)","refs":"","body":"* (feat) Adopt ESLint 9 and the shared @openmrs/eslint-config\n\nThis is the pilot migration for @openmrs/eslint-config, the new shared\nflat-config package that centralizes the ESLint rules that have been\ncopy-pasted and drifting across the openmrs-esm-* repositories. Since the\nconfig's base preset was ported from this repo's .eslintrc, esm-core is\nthe natural first adopter.\n\nWhat changed:\n\n- Bumped eslint from ^8.55.0 to ^9.13.0 (resolves to 9.39.5) and added\n  @openmrs/eslint-config. Removed the seven ESLint plugin devDependencies\n  the shared config now provides.\n- Replaced .eslintrc and .eslintignore with an eslint.config.mjs that\n  spreads the shared config. Flat config also stops config discovery at\n  the project root, which the old .eslintrc never did (it lacked\n  'root: true' and would cascade into parent directories).\n- Dropped '--ext ts,tsx' from the 28 workspace lint scripts, since the\n  flag was removed in ESLint 9 and flat config makes it unnecessary.\n- Removed 20 stale eslint-disable directives across 15 files. ESLint 9\n  reports unused directives by default, where v8 silently ignored them.\n  Most were artifacts of the typescript-eslint v8 rule renames\n  (ban-types was split, no-var-requires was folded into\n  no-require-imports) that the legacy config never accounted for. These\n  are comment and whitespace-only changes.\n- Updated turbo.json's lint cache input to point at eslint.config.mjs,\n  removed dependabot's now-resolved 'ESLint v9 requires flat config\n  migration' ignores, pointed its linting group at eslint and\n  @openmrs/eslint-config, and refreshed the copilot instructions.\n\nAll 30 workspaces lint green with no errors and no warnings, and a\nroot-level 'eslint --max-warnings 0' run (what lint-staged executes,\nincluding the e2e specs) exits clean, so adopting the shared config\nintroduced no new findings.\n\n* Hash all linted files in turbo's lint task inputs\n\nWith flat config, 'eslint src' lints JavaScript files too, but the lint\ntask only hashed src/**/*.{ts,tsx}. In practice turbo 2.5.2 still\ninvalidated the cache on .js changes (its hashing treats the glob more\npermissively than its dry-run input listing reports), but that safety\nlooks accidental, so this makes the inputs match what actually gets\nlinted. Also adds the .storybook and mocks directories that the\nstorybook workspace lints, which were never covered by src/**.\n\n* Add a changeset for the ESLint 9 migration\n\nPatch-level for the packages whose published source changed. The changes\nare comment-only removals of stale eslint-disable directives, so there is\nno functional impact on consumers.\n\n* Regenerate the API docs\n\nRemoving the stale eslint-disable comment lines shifted source line\nnumbers, and the generated docs embed 'Defined in' links with line\nanchors. All 42 changed files are line-number link updates only.","authorName":"Dennis Kigen","authorEmail":"kigen.work@gmail.com"},{"hash":"6c6f9d29ae785c34c45e1a1cad7b418fde07677c","date":"2026-06-08T16:40:57+03:00","message":"(feat) Prevent the shared SWR cache being torn down when a decorated component unmounts (#1793)","refs":"","body":"","authorName":"Dennis Kigen","authorEmail":"kigen.work@gmail.com"},{"hash":"7a7e7a41fbfcecfdb65805e914d117f0b9b61480","date":"2026-02-12T13:37:57-05:00","message":"(chore): Bump the github-actions group with 7 updates (#1595)","refs":"","body":"Bumps the github-actions group with 7 updates:\n\n| Package | From | To |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| [actions/checkout](https://github.com/actions/checkout) | `4` | `6` |\n| [preactjs/compressed-size-action](https://github.com/preactjs/compressed-size-action) | `2` | `3` |\n| [actions/setup-node](https://github.com/actions/setup-node) | `4` | `6` |\n| [actions/cache](https://github.com/actions/cache) | `4` | `5` |\n| [actions/upload-artifact](https://github.com/actions/upload-artifact) | `4` | `6` |\n| [fjogeleit/http-request-action](https://github.com/fjogeleit/http-request-action) | `1` | `2` |\n| [github/codeql-action](https://github.com/github/codeql-action) | `3` | `4` |\n\n\nUpdates `actions/checkout` from 4 to 6\n- [Release notes](https://github.com/actions/checkout/releases)\n- [Changelog](https://github.com/actions/checkout/blob/main/CHANGELOG.md)\n- [Commits](https://github.com/actions/checkout/compare/v4...v6)\n\nUpdates `preactjs/compressed-size-action` from 2 to 3\n- [Release notes](https://github.com/preactjs/compressed-size-action/releases)\n- [Commits](https://github.com/preactjs/compressed-size-action/compare/v2...v3)\n\nUpdates `actions/setup-node` from 4 to 6\n- [Release notes](https://github.com/actions/setup-node/releases)\n- [Commits](https://github.com/actions/setup-node/compare/v4...v6)\n\nUpdates `actions/cache` from 4 to 5\n- [Release notes](https://github.com/actions/cache/releases)\n- [Changelog](https://github.com/actions/cache/blob/main/RELEASES.md)\n- [Commits](https://github.com/actions/cache/compare/v4...v5)\n\nUpdates `actions/upload-artifact` from 4 to 6\n- [Release notes](https://github.com/actions/upload-artifact/releases)\n- [Commits](https://github.com/actions/upload-artifact/compare/v4...v6)\n\nUpdates `fjogeleit/http-request-action` from 1 to 2\n- [Release notes](https://github.com/fjogeleit/http-request-action/releases)\n- [Changelog](https://github.com/fjogeleit/http-request-action/blob/main/RELEASE.md)\n- [Commits](https://github.com/fjogeleit/http-request-action/compare/v1...v2)\n\nUpdates `github/codeql-action` from 3 to 4\n- [Release notes](https://github.com/github/codeql-action/releases)\n- [Changelog](https://github.com/github/codeql-action/blob/main/CHANGELOG.md)\n- [Commits](https://github.com/github/codeql-action/compare/v3...v4)\n\n---\nupdated-dependencies:\n- dependency-name: actions/checkout\n  dependency-version: '6'\n  dependency-type: direct:production\n  update-type: version-update:semver-major\n  dependency-group: github-actions\n- dependency-name: preactjs/compressed-size-action\n  dependency-version: '3'\n  dependency-type: direct:production\n  update-type: version-update:semver-major\n  dependency-group: github-actions\n- dependency-name: actions/setup-node\n  dependency-version: '6'\n  dependency-type: direct:production\n  update-type: version-update:semver-major\n  dependency-group: github-actions\n- dependency-name: actions/cache\n  dependency-version: '5'\n  dependency-type: direct:production\n  update-type: version-update:semver-major\n  dependency-group: github-actions\n- dependency-name: actions/upload-artifact\n  dependency-version: '6'\n  dependency-type: direct:production\n  update-type: version-update:semver-major\n  dependency-group: github-actions\n- dependency-name: fjogeleit/http-request-action\n  dependency-version: '2'\n  dependency-type: direct:production\n  update-type: version-update:semver-major\n  dependency-group: github-actions\n- dependency-name: github/codeql-action\n  dependency-version: '4'\n  dependency-type: direct:production\n  update-type: version-update:semver-major\n  dependency-group: github-actions\n...\n\nSigned-off-by: dependabot[bot] <support@github.com>\nCo-authored-by: dependabot[bot] <49699333+dependabot[bot]@users.noreply.github.com>","authorName":"dependabot[bot]","authorEmail":"49699333+dependabot[bot]@users.noreply.github.com"},{"hash":"ae58e27f6f114f5cf9b51a5786da6638471fec59","date":"2025-06-12T13:41:05-04:00","message":"(BREAKING) Use a single global cache instance for SWR (#1397)","refs":"","body":"","authorName":"Ian","authorEmail":"52504170+ibacher@users.noreply.github.com"}],"totalCount":9}"}]}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"bfb465e4-c8b2-4b61-a545-94b7863839b7","uuid":"f2dfadfc-9a80-4d64-97dc-57baa11657ef","timestamp":"2026-10-23T18:04:49.002Z","tool_use_result":[{"type":"text","text":"{"commits":[{"hash":"14197959572c1be0268228ebe25612161a3b6412","date":"2026-09-30T20:02:41+03:00","message":"(fix) Clear the shared SWR cache on logout (#1919)","refs":"","body":"* (fix) Clear the shared SWR cache on logout\n\nLogout called SWR's global `mutate`, which targets SWR's default cache\nrather than the shared cache that `openmrsComponentDecorator` provides to\nO3 apps. Logout navigates to the login page without a reload, so the\nprevious user's cached data survived into the next session in the same\ntab and rendered before revalidating.\n\nRedirectLogout now passes `cache` and `mutate` from `useSWRConfig()` to\n`performLogout`, which clears every cached key by name. Clearing by name\nis needed because a key-filter `mutate(() => true)` skips the\n`useSWRInfinite` and `useSWRSubscription` keys.\n\n* Clear the SWR cache before the early login redirect\n\nlogout() marks the session as logged out before it resolves. That\nre-runs the RedirectLogout effect, which redirects to the login page\nbefore performLogout has cleared the cache. Clear the cache in that\nbranch too, right before redirecting.\n\n* Mark the early cache clear as intentionally unawaited\n\nThe unauthenticated branch starts the SWR cache clear without awaiting\nit, because SWR updates the cache synchronously and the redirect only\nneeds that update. Mark the promise with `void` so it reads as\ndeliberately ignored rather than forgotten.","authorName":"Dennis Kigen","authorEmail":"kigen.work@gmail.com"},{"hash":"7cf6fef6986bc68a6fa55c2f56ec96f399271527","date":"2026-09-28T23:25:32+03:00","message":"(fix) Stop the E2E dependency caches from overwriting each other","refs":"","body":"Scope each node_modules cache in the E2E workflow to its own repo. The\nesm-core caches now exclude e2e_repo/**, and the cache for the checked-out\nrepo only covers e2e_repo/**/node_modules and includes the repo name in its\nkey.\n\nBoth caches used to cache **/node_modules from the workspace root, so each\none matched esm-core's node_modules as well as e2e_repo's. Restoring the\nother repo's cache overwrote esm-core's fresh install with the esm-core\nnode_modules saved alongside it, and the esm-core cache step then saved\nthat mixed tree under esm-core's lockfile key.\n\nAfter the turbo upgrade, the patient-chart cache still held esm-core's\npre-upgrade node_modules. It was restored over the new install and saved\nas main's esm-core cache. Runs that restored that entry skipped yarn\ninstall, and yarn turbo failed with \"Couldn't find a script named turbo\"\nbecause node_modules/.yarn-state.yml still described turbo 2.5.2.\n\ndeploy-pages uses the same path list as the E2E esm-core cache so the two\nkeep sharing entries. Changing the paths also changes the cache version,\nso entries saved with the old paths are no longer restored.\n","authorName":"Dennis Kigen","authorEmail":"kigen.work@gmail.com"},{"hash":"fb886e7a893d1638bb65ea0136967c99029ac54b","date":"2026-09-18T20:22:04+03:00","message":"(feat) O3-5986: Let attachments be recorded on and read by encounter (#1887)","refs":"","body":"* (feat) O3-5986: Let attachments be recorded on and read by encounter\n\ncreateAttachment now takes an optional encounter UUID and sends it as the\n`encounter` form field. That lets the visit note form record an image on the\nnote's own encounter instead of leaving it encounterless, which is why saved\nimages never show up again when we reopen the note.\n\ngetAttachments and useAttachments take the same optional UUID and hit\n`/attachment?patient=...&encounter=...` when it's set. We leave\nincludeEncounterless out of that request on purpose: the attachments module\nignores the encounter filter whenever includeEncounterless is present. Both\ngo through a new getAttachmentsUrl helper so the fetch and the SWR cache key\nare always the same string, and consumers can build that key when they need\nto invalidate it.\n\nExisting callers are unchanged. Adds the first tests for these helpers,\nmirrors the helper in the emr-api and storybook mocks and regenerates the\nAPI docs.\n\n* Skip the attachments fetch while the patient UUID is empty\n\nuseAttachments now passes a null SWR key when patientUuid is falsy, the same\nway usePatient does, so a form can defer the request until it knows which\nencounter to load.\n\n* Warn about unresolvable encounter UUIDs in the attachment docs\n\nThe attachments module resolves the encounter param with getEncounterByUuid\nand, when that yields null with no includeEncounterless flag, falls back to\nevery attachment of the patient. Callers should only pass an encounter UUID\nthey have already loaded.","authorName":"Dennis Kigen","authorEmail":"kigen.work@gmail.com"},{"hash":"92bf2449a4eef5836fbb8abd20fbb6d752633ea6","date":"2026-09-18T12:56:05-04:00","message":"(chore) Switch to using GitHub Actions cache for Actions","refs":"","body":"","authorName":"Ian","authorEmail":"ian.c.bacher@gmail.com"},{"hash":"eef2c97e8feb401ed3f5a5951ceaca1a0418bbe9","date":"2026-08-28T15:47:12-04:00","message":"(fix) Import map and routes should be cached (#1855)","refs":"","body":"Co-authored-by: Dennis Kigen <kigen.work@gmail.com>","authorName":"Ian","authorEmail":"52504170+ibacher@users.noreply.github.com"},{"hash":"8aa137ceb1785269c8c2636ac225f69dcbda3181","date":"2026-08-04T23:19:08+03:00","message":"(feat) Adopt ESLint 9 and the shared @openmrs/eslint-config (#1827)","refs":"","body":"* (feat) Adopt ESLint 9 and the shared @openmrs/eslint-config\n\nThis is the pilot migration for @openmrs/eslint-config, the new shared\nflat-config package that centralizes the ESLint rules that have been\ncopy-pasted and drifting across the openmrs-esm-* repositories. Since the\nconfig's base preset was ported from this repo's .eslintrc, esm-core is\nthe natural first adopter.\n\nWhat changed:\n\n- Bumped eslint from ^8.55.0 to ^9.13.0 (resolves to 9.39.5) and added\n  @openmrs/eslint-config. Removed the seven ESLint plugin devDependencies\n  the shared config now provides.\n- Replaced .eslintrc and .eslintignore with an eslint.config.mjs that\n  spreads the shared config. Flat config also stops config discovery at\n  the project root, which the old .eslintrc never did (it lacked\n  'root: true' and would cascade into parent directories).\n- Dropped '--ext ts,tsx' from the 28 workspace lint scripts, since the\n  flag was removed in ESLint 9 and flat config makes it unnecessary.\n- Removed 20 stale eslint-disable directives across 15 files. ESLint 9\n  reports unused directives by default, where v8 silently ignored them.\n  Most were artifacts of the typescript-eslint v8 rule renames\n  (ban-types was split, no-var-requires was folded into\n  no-require-imports) that the legacy config never accounted for. These\n  are comment and whitespace-only changes.\n- Updated turbo.json's lint cache input to point at eslint.config.mjs,\n  removed dependabot's now-resolved 'ESLint v9 requires flat config\n  migration' ignores, pointed its linting group at eslint and\n  @openmrs/eslint-config, and refreshed the copilot instructions.\n\nAll 30 workspaces lint green with no errors and no warnings, and a\nroot-level 'eslint --max-warnings 0' run (what lint-staged executes,\nincluding the e2e specs) exits clean, so adopting the shared config\nintroduced no new findings.\n\n* Hash all linted files in turbo's lint task inputs\n\nWith flat config, 'eslint src' lints JavaScript files too, but the lint\ntask only hashed src/**/*.{ts,tsx}. In practice turbo 2.5.2 still\ninvalidated the cache on .js changes (its hashing treats the glob more\npermissively than its dry-run input listing reports), but that safety\nlooks accidental, so this makes the inputs match what actually gets\nlinted. Also adds the .storybook and mocks directories that the\nstorybook workspace lints, which were never covered by src/**.\n\n* Add a changeset for the ESLint 9 migration\n\nPatch-level for the packages whose published source changed. The changes\nare comment-only removals of stale eslint-disable directives, so there is\nno functional impact on consumers.\n\n* Regenerate the API docs\n\nRemoving the stale eslint-disable comment lines shifted source line\nnumbers, and the generated docs embed 'Defined in' links with line\nanchors. All 42 changed files are line-number link updates only.","authorName":"Dennis Kigen","authorEmail":"kigen.work@gmail.com"},{"hash":"6c6f9d29ae785c34c45e1a1cad7b418fde07677c","date":"2026-06-08T16:40:57+03:00","message":"(feat) Prevent the shared SWR cache being torn down when a decorated component unmounts (#1793)","refs":"","body":"","authorName":"Dennis Kigen","authorEmail":"kigen.work@gmail.com"},{"hash":"7a7e7a41fbfcecfdb65805e914d117f0b9b61480","date":"2026-02-12T13:37:57-05:00","message":"(chore): Bump the github-actions group with 7 updates (#1595)","refs":"","body":"Bumps the github-actions group with 7 updates:\n\n| Package | From | To |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| [actions/checkout](https://github.com/actions/checkout) | `4` | `6` |\n| [preactjs/compressed-size-action](https://github.com/preactjs/compressed-size-action) | `2` | `3` |\n| [actions/setup-node](https://github.com/actions/setup-node) | `4` | `6` |\n| [actions/cache](https://github.com/actions/cache) | `4` | `5` |\n| [actions/upload-artifact](https://github.com/actions/upload-artifact) | `4` | `6` |\n| [fjogeleit/http-request-action](https://github.com/fjogeleit/http-request-action) | `1` | `2` |\n| [github/codeql-action](https://github.com/github/codeql-action) | `3` | `4` |\n\n\nUpdates `actions/checkout` from 4 to 6\n- [Release notes](https://github.com/actions/checkout/releases)\n- [Changelog](https://github.com/actions/checkout/blob/main/CHANGELOG.md)\n- [Commits](https://github.com/actions/checkout/compare/v4...v6)\n\nUpdates `preactjs/compressed-size-action` from 2 to 3\n- [Release notes](https://github.com/preactjs/compressed-size-action/releases)\n- [Commits](https://github.com/preactjs/compressed-size-action/compare/v2...v3)\n\nUpdates `actions/setup-node` from 4 to 6\n- [Release notes](https://github.com/actions/setup-node/releases)\n- [Commits](https://github.com/actions/setup-node/compare/v4...v6)\n\nUpdates `actions/cache` from 4 to 5\n- [Release notes](https://github.com/actions/cache/releases)\n- [Changelog](https://github.com/actions/cache/blob/main/RELEASES.md)\n- [Commits](https://github.com/actions/cache/compare/v4...v5)\n\nUpdates `actions/upload-artifact` from 4 to 6\n- [Release notes](https://github.com/actions/upload-artifact/releases)\n- [Commits](https://github.com/actions/upload-artifact/compare/v4...v6)\n\nUpdates `fjogeleit/http-request-action` from 1 to 2\n- [Release notes](https://github.com/fjogeleit/http-request-action/releases)\n- [Changelog](https://github.com/fjogeleit/http-request-action/blob/main/RELEASE.md)\n- [Commits](https://github.com/fjogeleit/http-request-action/compare/v1...v2)\n\nUpdates `github/codeql-action` from 3 to 4\n- [Release notes](https://github.com/github/codeql-action/releases)\n- [Changelog](https://github.com/github/codeql-action/blob/main/CHANGELOG.md)\n- [Commits](https://github.com/github/codeql-action/compare/v3...v4)\n\n---\nupdated-dependencies:\n- dependency-name: actions/checkout\n  dependency-version: '6'\n  dependency-type: direct:production\n  update-type: version-update:semver-major\n  dependency-group: github-actions\n- dependency-name: preactjs/compressed-size-action\n  dependency-version: '3'\n  dependency-type: direct:production\n  update-type: version-update:semver-major\n  dependency-group: github-actions\n- dependency-name: actions/setup-node\n  dependency-version: '6'\n  dependency-type: direct:production\n  update-type: version-update:semver-major\n  dependency-group: github-actions\n- dependency-name: actions/cache\n  dependency-version: '5'\n  dependency-type: direct:production\n  update-type: version-update:semver-major\n  dependency-group: github-actions\n- dependency-name: actions/upload-artifact\n  dependency-version: '6'\n  dependency-type: direct:production\n  update-type: version-update:semver-major\n  dependency-group: github-actions\n- dependency-name: fjogeleit/http-request-action\n  dependency-version: '2'\n  dependency-type: direct:production\n  update-type: version-update:semver-major\n  dependency-group: github-actions\n- dependency-name: github/codeql-action\n  dependency-version: '4'\n  dependency-type: direct:production\n  update-type: version-update:semver-major\n  dependency-group: github-actions\n...\n\nSigned-off-by: dependabot[bot] <support@github.com>\nCo-authored-by: dependabot[bot] <49699333+dependabot[bot]@users.noreply.github.com>","authorName":"dependabot[bot]","authorEmail":"49699333+dependabot[bot]@users.noreply.github.com"},{"hash":"ae58e27f6f114f5cf9b51a5786da6638471fec59","date":"2025-06-12T13:41:05-04:00","message":"(BREAKING) Use a single global cache instance for SWR (#1397)","refs":"","body":"","authorName":"Ian","authorEmail":"52504170+ibacher@users.noreply.github.com"}],"totalCount":9}"}],"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_01WkovkBX5NSMPf8HUfpgnG3","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"rule"}}]}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-haiku-5-5","id":"msg_011CgKcQ1h4RYwALbAKDsbyK","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01XnYuZhMQF5Vqxjn4PcVcqY","name":"mcp__falkon__list_commits","input":{"repo":"github.com/openmrs/openmrs-esm-patient-management","query":"search","since":"2026-01-01","perPage":30},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":15707,"cache_read_input_tokens":19777,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":15707},"output_tokens":3,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"bfb465e4-c8b2-4b61-a545-94b7863839b7","uuid":"d9d9b6c1-373f-46eb-aa9e-24d7439874ee","timestamp":"2026-10-23T18:04:49.259Z","request_id":"req_011CgKcQ1LiV9fRiKYSo8aCx","wire_tool_inputs":{"toolu_01XnYuZhMQF5Vqxjn4PcVcqY":{"repo":"github.com/openmrs/openmrs-esm-patient-management","query":"search","since":"2026-01-01","perPage":30}},"tool_use_meta":[{"id":"toolu_01XnYuZhMQF5Vqxjn4PcVcqY","display_name":"List Commits","server_display_name":"falkon-mcp-server","tool_name":"list_commits"}]}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01XnYuZhMQF5Vqxjn4PcVcqY","type":"tool_result","content":[{"type":"text","text":"{"commits":[{"hash":"7fc1a562ee45f4fabc38f3d04da6cbb6a6d7274a","date":"2026-09-30T19:52:25+03:00","message":"(chore) Remove leftover workspace v1 containers (#2790)","refs":"","body":"Removes the v1 WorkspaceContainer from the appointments patient overview,\nbed management, home, patient lists and patient search apps. These apps\nalready use workspace v2, which the app shell renders on its own, so the\ncontainers render nothing today.\n\nopenmrs-esm-core#1893 removes WorkspaceContainer from the framework. Once\nthat ships, these imports resolve to undefined and rendering them crashes\nthe page's root component.\n\nAlso drops an unused DefaultWorkspaceProps type import from the ward\ncancel admission request test.","authorName":"Dennis Kigen","authorEmail":"kigen.work@gmail.com"},{"hash":"df9d1478f6786ca65541f1a6b6ffdb91f8223fb2","date":"2026-09-29T10:09:26-04:00","message":"(BREAKING) O3-6012: Remove the patient-search-button extension and v1 patient-search-workspace (#2773)","refs":"","body":"","authorName":"chibongho","authorEmail":"cbho@pih.org"},{"hash":"8eff6bab5486b7773d3cb7aa17e4cc310fa7715d","date":"2026-09-29T01:58:55+03:00","message":"(fix) Declare react-dom as a peer dependency (#2784)","refs":"","body":"Add react-dom 18.x to peerDependencies in the bed management, patient list management, patient registration, patient search, service queues, and ward apps.\n\nThe app shell provides react-dom through module federation, but the\nOpenMRS rspack config only shares the dependencies an app lists in\npeerDependencies. Without react-dom listed there, the app loads the\ncopy of react-dom bundled into its own build instead of the shell's.","authorName":"Dennis Kigen","authorEmail":"kigen.work@gmail.com"},{"hash":"b322ea70dcbc8614774d7b363ca1abca07fe07f0","date":"2026-09-28T19:04:17+03:00","message":"(fix) O3-5914: Preserve saved location attributes while searching (#2778)","refs":"","body":"","authorName":"Dennis Kigen","authorEmail":"kigen.work@gmail.com"},{"hash":"fd828fc942602c9fe4142211da86ada5005b614a","date":"2026-09-16T16:22:16+03:00","message":"(test) O3-2741: Add E2E tests for the dedicated patient search page (#2747)","refs":"","body":"Add E2E coverage for navigation to the dedicated patient search page, patient selection, sex and birth-year filters, and resetting filters.\n\nIntroduce a patient search page object and share patient-name extraction with the existing navbar search tests.","authorName":"Veronica Mukuhi Muthee","authorEmail":"veronica.mukuhi@gmail.com"},{"hash":"5a85ebcd3d573d168ac404e5b39f1cc06a3dec32","date":"2026-09-15T11:12:17+03:00","message":"(fix) O3-5877: Show a clear message when patient search query is below the minimum character count (#2667)","refs":"","body":"","authorName":"solomonfortune","authorEmail":"solomonbuwule@gmail.com"},{"hash":"ac5758f3ba0c6868eb414e715e279e3e9d96ee90","date":"2026-09-14T15:55:43-04:00","message":"(fix) Make patient search a little more light-weight (#2742)","refs":"","body":"Basically this does two things:\n\n1. Fetch a smaller representation for a visit that includes the minimum\n   we need.\n2. Makes the SWR cache hold visits returned for 3 minutes. The idea\n   being that paging through a single search shouldn't need to refetch\n   the visit status unless the user genuinely switches their attention\n   to elsewhere.","authorName":"Ian","authorEmail":"52504170+ibacher@users.noreply.github.com"},{"hash":"dab9f79eef9f57aeee91bd237c0d6431cd9c4f43","date":"2026-09-10T20:50:28+03:00","message":"(fix) Tell the user when the refine filters, not the query, emptied the search results (#2725)","refs":"","body":"* (fix) Tell the user when the refine filters, not the query, emptied the search results\n\nWhen a refine filter matched nothing, the results area showed the same message as a query with no hits, \"Sorry, no patient charts were found\" with a hint to retry with the patient's ID. That points the user at the wrong fix. When the query found patients and the filters removed all of them, the empty state now reads \"No patients match these filters\" with a hint to remove or change a filter, following the filter empty states in the queues, active visits, patient lists and ward apps. A query that itself found nothing keeps the original message.\n\n* Keep loading until every page has landed before blaming the filters\n\nThe filters run over the rows loaded so far, and a broad search arrives in waves. After page 1 lands, isLoading is false while later pages are still in flight, so a filter that only matches a later page showed \"No patients match these filters\" until that page arrived. The results now stay in the loading state while the filtered set is empty and pages are still arriving, and the message appears only once loading has settled. Between waves isValidating drops for a render before the next wave is requested, so the check also compares the pages needed with the pages requested.\n\n* docs: clarify translated empty-state props\n\nDocument that the empty-state title and hint expect already translated strings, and describe their default messages.","authorName":"Dennis Kigen","authorEmail":"kigen.work@gmail.com"},{"hash":"d544f28a430707feba18e7f8b22f2c1b106577e5","date":"2026-09-10T13:27:53+03:00","message":"(fix) Open header patient search results with Enter (#2729)","refs":"","body":"* fix: open header search results with Enter\n\nSelect the focused patient from the displayed search or recently viewed\nlist instead of expecting an array from the keyboard hook. Align the\ncallback type with the hook and preserve advanced-page form submission.\n\n* Reset stale header search selection\n\nClear the keyboard index when the query changes or the focused patient\nis replaced. Preserve it when background refreshes or appended pages keep\nthe same patient at that index. Cover the transitions with rendered tests.","authorName":"Dennis Kigen","authorEmail":"kigen.work@gmail.com"},{"hash":"fcb7a36a901fe4e7072a88dd88e6b6dd1ea72627","date":"2026-09-08T19:51:50+03:00","message":"(fix) Preserve patient search results when clearing attribute filters (#2728)","refs":"","body":"Normalize cleared concept and location selections to an empty string so\nthey are no longer treated as active filters. Cover clearing and applying\nboth field types with regression tests, including missing attributes.","authorName":"Dennis Kigen","authorEmail":"kigen.work@gmail.com"},{"hash":"aa2f12e1960da9ef145339b63478c59ab1df5afe","date":"2026-09-04T16:28:00+03:00","message":"(fix) Pluralise the refine search filter counts and label the forms (#2719)","refs":"","body":"* (fix) Pluralise the refine search filter counts and label the forms\n\nThe Apply button read \"1 filters applied\" because the singular form in en.json carried the plural text. The tablet banner built its sentence from a count in one element and \"search queries added\" in another, which read \"1 search queries added\" and gave translators no way to reorder or pluralise it. The banner now renders one translatable sentence with proper plural forms, keeping the count badge.\n\nThe refine search forms declared role=\"refine-search\" and role=\"refine-search-tablet\", which are not ARIA roles and hide the form semantics assistive technology would otherwise announce. Each form is now labelled by its own heading instead, so it is announced as the \"Refine search\" form.\n\n* Use generated ids for the refine search form labels and keep mock interpolation literal\n\nThe form labels used fixed element ids, which collide when two refine search forms are mounted at once, as they are on the tablet search page today. React's useId gives each instance its own id.\n\nThe test mock's interpolation passed the value straight to String.replace, which would interpret dollar-sign sequences in a value as replacement tokens. A callback keeps the value literal.","authorName":"Dennis Kigen","authorEmail":"kigen.work@gmail.com"},{"hash":"4d8121f988869a859c12afada7ca29039a924486","date":"2026-09-04T14:22:21+03:00","message":"(fix) Apply the configured age bounds to the refine search age field (#2720)","refs":"","body":"* (fix) Apply the configured age bounds to the refine search age field\n\nThe config schema has offered `searchFilterFields.age.min` and `max` since the person attribute filters landed, and the age field reads them, but neither field builder ever passed them through: the built-in fields were created with only a name and a type. Setting the values did nothing. Both the desktop panel and the tablet dialog now hand the configured bounds to the field.\n\nA maximum of 0, the schema default, means no maximum. Carbon marks any value above `max` invalid, so passing 0 through would have flagged every age.\n\n* Explain an out-of-range age\n\nCarbon only draws the invalid border and icon for a value outside min and max. Without invalidText the user gets no reason, so the field now says which range the configured bounds allow.\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Nethmi Rodrigo <nethmi@openmrs.org>","authorName":"Dennis Kigen","authorEmail":"kigen.work@gmail.com"},{"hash":"d4d67713e8b9228e90210e122b1054de4f822bd3","date":"2026-09-04T14:20:28+03:00","message":"(fix) O3-5917: Keep newly added relationship rows correctly associated (#2721)","refs":"","body":"New relationship rows have no server uuid, so every new row rendered with the same undefined React key and React reconciled them by position. The relationship type select was also uncontrolled (defaultValue). After removing one of two new rows, the surviving row kept showing the removed row's person and type while Formik held the other row's values.\n\nGive each new relationship a client-side id when it is pushed, key rows on the server uuid or that id, and drive the select from its Formik value. The id is never sent to the server: saveRelationships only picks the fields it needs.\n\nThe section test's fetchPerson mock returned a response object where the real function returns an array, so no test could exercise the person search. Fix the mock, add an interaction test that fills two rows, removes the first, and checks the second, and fail any test in the file that logs a React key warning.","authorName":"Dennis Kigen","authorEmail":"kigen.work@gmail.com"},{"hash":"cca993b14d3d33cea16a18112dcb4179e1632971","date":"2026-09-04T14:11:29+03:00","message":"(fix) Stop the header search icon opening a second overlay on the tablet search page (#2723)","refs":"","body":"* (fix) Stop the header search icon opening a second overlay on the tablet search page\n\nOn tablet, the search page renders the patient search overlay itself. The header search icon also forces its own overlay open whenever the route is the search page, so the page mounted two complete overlays stacked at the same position: two result lists, two search inputs and two refine forms, each with its own state. The one on top was the page's, so the icon's copy did nothing but duplicate every request and render.\n\nThe icon now only opens its input on the search page in desktop layouts, and renders nothing at all on that page in tablet layouts, where the page's overlay already carries the search input and its own back button. What users see is unchanged.\n\n* Keep the icon's overlay on the phone search page\n\nThe page only renders its own overlay in the tablet layout, so suppressing the icon for every non-desktop layout left phone users on the search page with no search input at all. The icon now steps aside only where the page renders an overlay.\n\n* (test) Clean up patient search icon test setup\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Nethmi Rodrigo <nethmi@openmrs.org>","authorName":"Dennis Kigen","authorEmail":"kigen.work@gmail.com"},{"hash":"5aa90304637d46e0536cf8e6343c2aed296f30a2","date":"2026-09-03T23:53:04+03:00","message":"(fix) Keep the header search input in step with the query in the URL (#2718)","refs":"","body":"On the search page the header search input is seeded from the query in the URL, but only once, when it mounts. A browser back or forward, or a link to another query, changed the results and the heading while the input kept showing the previous term. The compact search and the search bar now follow the term they are given whenever it changes.","authorName":"Dennis Kigen","authorEmail":"kigen.work@gmail.com"},{"hash":"b560585f10a4d207b7d7bdb204857711eb24ad41","date":"2026-09-03T23:30:55+03:00","message":"(test) Assert the search paging tests through what the user sees (#2716)","refs":"","body":"The paging tests stubbed the result views and asserted on attributes of the stubs: which uuid slice was handed to PatientSearchResults, and test ids for the empty and error states. The framework mock stubs the banner's internals, so a real banner cannot show a patient's name in tests. The results stub now renders each patient's name instead, and the empty and error states are the real components, so the assertions read the names and messages a user would see.\n\nThe 1700-result test proves the last page is reachable the way a user would: filter by a postcode only the last patient has and expect that patient to be shown. The error test asserts that no request follows the error state, instead of comparing start indexes against a copy of the component's wave size. The wave test bounds concurrency between one page and the whole set rather than mirroring that constant.\n\nThe file runs under jsdom because the refine-search form submit does not fire under happy-dom, matching advanced-patient-search.test.tsx.","authorName":"Dennis Kigen","authorEmail":"kigen.work@gmail.com"},{"hash":"db742933dbb69eca1f422b45e4b99c82df886a32","date":"2026-09-03T23:22:37+03:00","message":"(fix) Match the birthdate filters against the stored date and trim the postcode filter (#2717)","refs":"","body":"The refine search date of birth filters parsed each patient's birthdate with `new Date` and read the local day, month and year. The backend serialises birthdates as midnight in its own timezone, so in a browser west of that timezone every patient shifted to the previous day and missed the filters, and a patient with no recorded birthdate became 1 January 1970 and matched filters for that date. The filters now read the calendar date off the string, and a patient without a birthdate matches no date of birth filter.\n\nThe postcode filter compared the typed value exactly, so a stray leading or trailing space matched nothing. It is trimmed when the filters are applied, which also keeps the applied-filter count honest for a whitespace-only value.","authorName":"Dennis Kigen","authorEmail":"kigen.work@gmail.com"},{"hash":"5d48e9e791aec4b8fce00334c974ebbee2fb8a9a","date":"2026-09-03T12:54:32+03:00","message":"(fix) Keep patient search on the selected page and load result pages in parallel (#2708)","refs":"","body":"","authorName":"Pius Rubangakene","authorEmail":"piruville@gmail.com"},{"hash":"4708bdfce312569c1b5939cc61b21d23ae7f1052","date":"2026-08-28T17:54:27-04:00","message":"(fix) Add memoization of search results and reduce secondary queries (#2702)","refs":"","body":"","authorName":"Ian","authorEmail":"52504170+ibacher@users.noreply.github.com"},{"hash":"7a2ccf502f6f557aa2628dee2371b2e70f8be5e3","date":"2026-08-27T18:52:46+08:00","message":"(feat) O3-5760: Rework Service Queues dashboard to match design (#2615)","refs":"","body":"* (feat) O3-5760: Rework Service Queues dashboard to match design\n\n* (fix) e2e tests\n\n* (fix) Address review feedback on queues dashboard rework\n\n* (fix) Address review on queues dashboard rework\n\n* (fix) Address review feedback on queues dashboard rework\n\n- Bound the average wait time to entries started today and render '--'\n  instead of 'NaN mins' when the backend has no completed waits to average\n- Surface loading and error states in the Attending section so a failed\n  request is no longer indistinguishable from nobody being attended\n- Cap the Attending cards at three behind a 'View all' toggle and say\n  'No one is being attended' explicitly when the list is empty\n- Exclude Cancelled/Completed/Missed appointments from the expected\n  appointments count and tab\n- Translate appointment statuses, use a single interpolated key for the\n  waiting list tab label, and use the framework age() helper so infants\n  no longer render as '0 years old'\n\n* (fix) O3-5760: Address second round of review feedback on queues dashboard\n\nAdds concepts.waitingStatusConceptUuid so the waiting list, its tab count and\nthe \"Waiting\" metric stop overloading defaultStatusConceptUuid, which only\ndescribes the status a newly created queue entry starts in. All three read the\nnew config, so the count cannot disagree with the rows beneath it.\n\n- Count the waiting list via queue-entry-metrics instead of paging through\n  every entry. useQueueEntriesMetrics now reports isLoading and error so the\n  tab label shows no momentary \"(0)\" before the request settles.\n- Drop useServiceMetricsCount: it hardcoded status=Waiting as a concept name\n  and has no remaining callers.\n- Send forDate as an ISO 8601 string. The appointments module's DateUtil does\n  not parse a ZZ numeric offset. The test now asserts the value, not the path.\n- Show the selected service in the header even when the location is \"All\",\n  since the modal permits that combination, and reset the service when the\n  default location resolves, as services are scoped to a location.\n- Look the expected-appointments name cell up through an id/patientUuid map\n  rather than scanning every row on each render.\n- Guard the service sort against a missing display, order attending-patients\n  imports components before hooks, and drop an unused @carbon/type import.\n\n* (fix) O3-5760: Trim the waitingStatusConceptUuid description\n\nIts contrast with defaultStatusConceptUuid belongs in review, not in the\nconfig reference that implementers read.\n\n* (fix) O3-5760: Scope the wait-time metric and Call action to the waiting status\n\n* (fix) O3-5760: Remove the appointments features from the dashboard\n\nThe Expected appointments tab and Appointments today card only match\nappointments whose location equals the selected queue location exactly,\nand the alternative leaks other locations' appointments. Dropping both\nuntil location tagging is settled.\n\nAlso formats Avg. wait time like the Wait time column, and shows --\nwhen the backend has nothing to average.\n\n* (fix) O3-5760: Round the average wait time before guarding on it\n\n* (fix) O3-5760: Send the wait-time window as UTC\n\nThe queue module parses startedOnOrAfter with a zone-less\nSimpleDateFormat, so browser-local midnight was read in the server's\ntimezone and hid everything queued before the client's offset elapsed.\n\n* (fix) O3-5760: Restructure the Attending card details\n\n* (fix) O3-5760: Move the service and priority into a card footer\n\nSeparates them from the demographics with a rule, service left and pill\nright, per design review. The card element is now the link itself rather\nthan a wrapper around one.\n\n* (fix) O3-5760: Count the entries a search leaves in the waiting list heading\n\n`totalCount` is the server's count of every waiting entry, so the heading kept\nreporting the full list while the table showed only the search results.\n\n* (fix) O3-5760: Send the metrics window as an unambiguous instant\n\nThe queue module could not parse a timezone offset, so browser-local midnight\nwas being converted to UTC and sent zone-less — correct only because servers\nusually run in UTC. openmrs-module-queue now parses REST date parameters with\nConversionUtil, so send an ISO-8601 instant and let the server resolve it.\n\nRequires queue module 3.1.0 or later.\n\n* (chore) Require queue module 3.1.0 for queue-entry-metrics\n\nThe average wait time card sends `startedOnOrAfter` as an ISO-8601 instant,\nwhich only queue 3.1.0 onwards parses, so declare that in the backend\ndependencies instead of noting it in a code comment. The `-0` prerelease\nfloor keeps SNAPSHOT builds valid for testing.\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Ujjawal Prabhat <ujjawal@Ujjawals-MacBook-Pro.local>\nCo-authored-by: jwnasambu <33891016+jwnasambu@users.noreply.github.com>\nCo-authored-by: Nethmi Rodrigo <nethmi@openmrs.org>","authorName":"Ujjawal Prabhat","authorEmail":"UjjawalPrabhat1@gmail.com"},{"hash":"0c695bcda73aa438cf88ba10cdddfe27ab22d590","date":"2026-07-30T14:22:27+08:00","message":"(feat) O3-5761: List checked-in patients before search when adding to queue (#2633)","refs":"","body":"* (feat) O3-5761: List checked-in patients before search when adding to queue\n\n* (feat) O3-5761: Render checked-in patients with the patient banner\n\nReuse the framework patient-banner components for the checked-in patients\nshortlist so its rows match patient-search results, and pass a mapped FHIR\npatient to the selection callback instead of a bare uuid.\n\n- Add mapActiveVisitPatientToFhir to convert the REST visit patient into the\n  minimal FHIR shape the banner components expect\n- Widen the useActiveVisits custom representation accordingly and fetch all\n  pages via useOpenmrsFetchAll so the list isn't truncated\n- Drop the restrictToToday parameter; the server-side fromStartDate filter\n  already scopes results to today\n- Move the config gate to AddPatientToQueueButton and rename the property to\n  showCheckedInPatientsBeforeSearch\n- Add loading and error states, and cover the new behaviour with tests\n\n* (chore) O3-5761: Clarify that the checked-in patients list is location-scoped\n\nThe queue-entry exclusion is filtered by the selected queue location, but the\ndoc comment and empty-state copy implied it covered any queue. Reword both to\nmatch the actual scope.\n\n* (chore) O3-5761: Pin the location scope of the checked-in patients exclusion\n\nThe shortlist filters active visits against queue entries scoped to the selected location, which is deliberate: a patient can legitimately hold entries at several locations, and the backend only rejects a repeat entry in the same queue. Nothing asserted the criteria passed to useQueueEntries, so that scope could have drifted silently.\n\n* (chore) translation changes\n\n* (chore) O3-5761: Clarify that the checked-in patients shortlist is today-only\n\nThe docblock said the list shows patients \"with an active visit\", but\nuseActiveVisits always sends fromStartDate=<today>, so an open visit that\nstarted before today is excluded. Spell out the today-only scope.\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: NethmiRodrigo <nethmi.dilinika@gmail.com>\nCo-authored-by: Ujjawal Prabhat <ujjawal@10-64-49-196.0200.binb.id.iosda.org>\nCo-authored-by: Nethmi Rodrigo <nethmi@openmrs.org>","authorName":"Ujjawal Prabhat","authorEmail":"UjjawalPrabhat1@gmail.com"},{"hash":"595e97286e45a540a4ddf72dbda646a3c01e78dc","date":"2026-07-27T16:42:07+03:00","message":"(feat) Improve no active visit empty state in admission workspace (#2172)","refs":"","body":"* feat: improve no active visit admission state\n\nShow a start visit prompt when a patient without an active visit is selected for admission.\n\nAdd scoped workspace styles and test coverage for the no active visit admission workflow.\n\n* Show admit and start visit buttons on ward admission patient search cards\n\nImplements the design agreed in the PR review discussion: in the Add\npatient to ward search, the patient card is no longer clickable. Patients\nwith an active visit get an enabled Admit button that opens the admission\nworkspace. Patients without one get a start visit button next to a\ndisabled Admit button, which enables in place once the visit is saved.\n\nThe patient search workspace gains an optional selectPatientButton prop\nso the ward can configure the button without leaking it into the other\nconsumers of the search workspace (appointments, patient lists, queues).\n\n* Pass the patient to the start visit button slot on search result cards\n\nThe banner rendered start-visit-button-slot2 without the patient in the\nslot state, so the start visit button launched the visit form with an\nundefined patient prop. The visit form and the extensions it hosts, like\nthe billing check-in form, dereference that patient, which surfaced as\nrequests to patient/undefined and post-save callback failures on billing\nenabled instances.\n\n* Give the admit patient workspace a footer and visit context\n\nThe workspace rendered its primary action as a ghost link floating in an\notherwise empty panel, with a back link of equal visual weight beneath it\nand no information beyond the patient banner. The admit and back actions\nnow sit in the standard workspace footer button bar, matching the bed\nselection form, and the body shows the active visit's type, location,\nand start time alongside the existing admission warnings.\n\nAdmitPatientButton accepts optional kind and size props so the footer can\nrender it as a primary action without changing its ghost styling in the\nadmission requests bench.\n\n* Auto-open the admission workspace after starting a visit\n\nAfter the visit form saves in the Add patient to ward flow, the admission\nworkspace now opens automatically for the same patient instead of\nreturning the user to the search results to click Admit. The callback\nflows from the ward's workspace props through the patient search context\nand banner into the visit form's onVisitStarted hook.\n\nLaunching a child workspace immediately after another closes previously\ntripped a lifecycle race in workspace2 that could mount the closed form's\ncomponent with the new workspace's props. That race was fixed in\nopenmrs/openmrs-esm-core#1807, which is included in the framework build\nthis branch resolves after rebasing onto main. Verified locally against\nthat build: repeated start-visit-then-admit flows land on the admission\nworkspace with no stale component mount and no patient/undefined\nrequests.\n\n* Use flex instead of hard-coded button widths in admission workspace footer\n\nCarbon's .cds--btn-set .cds--btn rule caps footer buttons at 196px and\nout-specifies a single CSS module class, which is why the previous rule\nneeded !important. Doubling the class wins on specificity instead, and\nflex: 1 splits the row evenly without hard-coding a 50% width. With two\nbuttons the layout is unchanged; in the error state the lone back button\nnow fills the footer instead of stopping at half width.\n\nAddresses review feedback from @ibacher.","authorName":"Dennis Kigen","authorEmail":"kigen.work@gmail.com"},{"hash":"e4aacbd5a6242821c4f956230535f598cdeac835","date":"2026-07-24T19:54:04-04:00","message":"(fix) Patient search should bypass service worker caching (#2638)","refs":"","body":"","authorName":"Ian","authorEmail":"52504170+ibacher@users.noreply.github.com"},{"hash":"39be6d5abb7182bd5b3e08b8684aefb6e046542f","date":"2026-06-01T17:40:34-04:00","message":"(feat) O3-5714: Improve performance with multi-paged patient search results (#2554)","refs":"","body":"* O3-5714: Improve performance with multi-paged patient search results\n\nSeveral notable fixes for the compact-patient-search component:\n\n* Previously, each call to `useSWRInfinite()` was, in essence, returning\n  new copies of existing data, which lead to unnecessary re-renders. This\n  has been fixed by setting `keepPreviousData` to `true`\n* Previously, when `useSWRInfinite()` set `isLoading` to `true`, all\n  results were replaced with placeholder. Since this gets set to `true`\n  even when, e.g., loading a second page of results, this resulted in\n  unnecessary unmounts and recreations, which was both a memory leak and\n  lead to a stampede of requests.\n* All search results were previously rendered and retained. This leads\n  to stampedes of secondary queries (e.g., for patient photos, queue\n  status, visit status, etc.). Instead, this PR moves us to using list\n  virtualization so that roughly 10-18 items are retained in a React\n  query. Large scrolls backwards or forwards have some slight glitches\n  as components are re-rendered, but the easiest way to fix this is in\n  the components rendering the secondary queries themselves.\n* Recent patients, however, are not virtualized at all, as we rely on\n  this being a limited list that is safe to load.\n* A mistake in the call to `useArrowNavigation()` resulted in the arrow\n  keys only being usable for up to the number of `recentPatients`\n* This PR adds additional component-level memoization where it makes\n  sense to speed up rendering. In addition, in the context of search\n  results, we re-tune SWR to more aggressively cache so that there's\n  less need to re-try, e.g., patient photo queries\n* Additionally, this PR makes two fixes the service queues banner tag.\n  First, if it is rendered outside the patient chart, a wrapper component\n  is used so no query needs to be issued. Second, the query that was\n  used overfetched data, especially as the queue details in the modal\n  are basically reloaded, so the representation has been updated to\n  minimize the data requested. This is one of the biggest contributing\n  components.\n\n* Fixes from code review\n\n* Address Copilot comment","authorName":"Ian","authorEmail":"52504170+ibacher@users.noreply.github.com"},{"hash":"eb42a62c491f87c2914681e5253b5c2e1af9144f","date":"2026-04-28T11:22:13+05:30","message":"(fix) O3-5634: Type safe patient search app (#2512)","refs":"","body":"","authorName":"Dilan Kavishka","authorEmail":"109354298+dilankavishka@users.noreply.github.com"},{"hash":"fb6d9a2a40f7b9b6e9c9f48ab99e5bc734c8fb49","date":"2026-03-27T17:25:47+03:00","message":"(fix) Improve patient search robustness and accessibility (#2404)","refs":"","body":"","authorName":"Dennis Kigen","authorEmail":"kigen.work@gmail.com"},{"hash":"bc06adf7eb92305b3f13849c196acb2a1869dff6","date":"2026-03-26T22:11:07+03:00","message":"(fix) Hide generic overflow actions in task-specific patient search pickers (#2409)","refs":"","body":"","authorName":"Dennis Kigen","authorEmail":"kigen.work@gmail.com"},{"hash":"219529a47911448f4f1fb357475102eddc5ed262","date":"2026-02-26T15:15:59+03:00","message":"(fix) Filter voided patients from recently viewed list (#2284)","refs":"","body":"The REST API returns voided patients when fetched by UUID (unlike the\nsearch endpoint, which excludes them server-side). This means voided\npatient UUIDs persisted in the user's patientsVisited property would\nstill render in the recently viewed list.\n\nAdd `voided` to the custom representation and filter voided patients\nin useRestPatients.","authorName":"Dennis Kigen","authorEmail":"kigen.work@gmail.com"},{"hash":"240d4728294a690aaf957f12320fed287bd4c6b7","date":"2026-01-26T12:04:18+03:00","message":"(feat) O3-5342: Add ability to search queue services  (#2192)","refs":"","body":"","authorName":"Laurent Ouma","authorEmail":"98098891+Omoshlawi@users.noreply.github.com"},{"hash":"2fe547d1f48f1d4c02db97737bd520831c6783f0","date":"2026-01-23T20:49:44+03:00","message":"(fix) Improve recently viewed patients feature behavior (#2221)","refs":"","body":"The recently viewed patients feature had several issues that could confuse\nusers and cause unnecessary network requests:\n\n1. When a user had no viewing history, the component rendered nothing instead\nof showing an empty state, leaving blank space in the UI.\n\n2. The showRecentlySearchedPatients config flag only controlled whether the UI\nwas displayed, but tracking (POST requests) and preloading still occurred even\nwhen disabled.\n\n3. Users could briefly see \"No recently viewed patients\" before their actual\nhistory loaded, due to a race condition between fetching user properties and\nrendering the empty state.\n\nThis commit:\n\n- Fixes blank UI when user has no recently viewed patients by adding fallback\nempty state for null data\n- Respects the feature flag for tracking and preload, not just UI display\n- Prevents premature empty state flash while user properties are loading\n- Updates empty state copy to \"No recently viewed patients\"\n- Uses custom:(userProperties) representation to preserve other properties on update\n\nThe feature now fails gracefully, fully respects its config flag, and shows accurate\nloading states.","authorName":"Dennis Kigen","authorEmail":"kigen.work@gmail.com"}],"totalCount":34}"}]}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"bfb465e4-c8b2-4b61-a545-94b7863839b7","uuid":"ae75e315-1052-4558-a1b5-0ba6305ce3e5","timestamp":"2026-10-23T18:04:49.356Z","tool_use_result":[{"type":"text","text":"{"commits":[{"hash":"7fc1a562ee45f4fabc38f3d04da6cbb6a6d7274a","date":"2026-09-30T19:52:25+03:00","message":"(chore) Remove leftover workspace v1 containers (#2790)","refs":"","body":"Removes the v1 WorkspaceContainer from the appointments patient overview,\nbed management, home, patient lists and patient search apps. These apps\nalready use workspace v2, which the app shell renders on its own, so the\ncontainers render nothing today.\n\nopenmrs-esm-core#1893 removes WorkspaceContainer from the framework. Once\nthat ships, these imports resolve to undefined and rendering them crashes\nthe page's root component.\n\nAlso drops an unused DefaultWorkspaceProps type import from the ward\ncancel admission request test.","authorName":"Dennis Kigen","authorEmail":"kigen.work@gmail.com"},{"hash":"df9d1478f6786ca65541f1a6b6ffdb91f8223fb2","date":"2026-09-29T10:09:26-04:00","message":"(BREAKING) O3-6012: Remove the patient-search-button extension and v1 patient-search-workspace (#2773)","refs":"","body":"","authorName":"chibongho","authorEmail":"cbho@pih.org"},{"hash":"8eff6bab5486b7773d3cb7aa17e4cc310fa7715d","date":"2026-09-29T01:58:55+03:00","message":"(fix) Declare react-dom as a peer dependency (#2784)","refs":"","body":"Add react-dom 18.x to peerDependencies in the bed management, patient list management, patient registration, patient search, service queues, and ward apps.\n\nThe app shell provides react-dom through module federation, but the\nOpenMRS rspack config only shares the dependencies an app lists in\npeerDependencies. Without react-dom listed there, the app loads the\ncopy of react-dom bundled into its own build instead of the shell's.","authorName":"Dennis Kigen","authorEmail":"kigen.work@gmail.com"},{"hash":"b322ea70dcbc8614774d7b363ca1abca07fe07f0","date":"2026-09-28T19:04:17+03:00","message":"(fix) O3-5914: Preserve saved location attributes while searching (#2778)","refs":"","body":"","authorName":"Dennis Kigen","authorEmail":"kigen.work@gmail.com"},{"hash":"fd828fc942602c9fe4142211da86ada5005b614a","date":"2026-09-16T16:22:16+03:00","message":"(test) O3-2741: Add E2E tests for the dedicated patient search page (#2747)","refs":"","body":"Add E2E coverage for navigation to the dedicated patient search page, patient selection, sex and birth-year filters, and resetting filters.\n\nIntroduce a patient search page object and share patient-name extraction with the existing navbar search tests.","authorName":"Veronica Mukuhi Muthee","authorEmail":"veronica.mukuhi@gmail.com"},{"hash":"5a85ebcd3d573d168ac404e5b39f1cc06a3dec32","date":"2026-09-15T11:12:17+03:00","message":"(fix) O3-5877: Show a clear message when patient search query is below the minimum character count (#2667)","refs":"","body":"","authorName":"solomonfortune","authorEmail":"solomonbuwule@gmail.com"},{"hash":"ac5758f3ba0c6868eb414e715e279e3e9d96ee90","date":"2026-09-14T15:55:43-04:00","message":"(fix) Make patient search a little more light-weight (#2742)","refs":"","body":"Basically this does two things:\n\n1. Fetch a smaller representation for a visit that includes the minimum\n   we need.\n2. Makes the SWR cache hold visits returned for 3 minutes. The idea\n   being that paging through a single search shouldn't need to refetch\n   the visit status unless the user genuinely switches their attention\n   to elsewhere.","authorName":"Ian","authorEmail":"52504170+ibacher@users.noreply.github.com"},{"hash":"dab9f79eef9f57aeee91bd237c0d6431cd9c4f43","date":"2026-09-10T20:50:28+03:00","message":"(fix) Tell the user when the refine filters, not the query, emptied the search results (#2725)","refs":"","body":"* (fix) Tell the user when the refine filters, not the query, emptied the search results\n\nWhen a refine filter matched nothing, the results area showed the same message as a query with no hits, \"Sorry, no patient charts were found\" with a hint to retry with the patient's ID. That points the user at the wrong fix. When the query found patients and the filters removed all of them, the empty state now reads \"No patients match these filters\" with a hint to remove or change a filter, following the filter empty states in the queues, active visits, patient lists and ward apps. A query that itself found nothing keeps the original message.\n\n* Keep loading until every page has landed before blaming the filters\n\nThe filters run over the rows loaded so far, and a broad search arrives in waves. After page 1 lands, isLoading is false while later pages are still in flight, so a filter that only matches a later page showed \"No patients match these filters\" until that page arrived. The results now stay in the loading state while the filtered set is empty and pages are still arriving, and the message appears only once loading has settled. Between waves isValidating drops for a render before the next wave is requested, so the check also compares the pages needed with the pages requested.\n\n* docs: clarify translated empty-state props\n\nDocument that the empty-state title and hint expect already translated strings, and describe their default messages.","authorName":"Dennis Kigen","authorEmail":"kigen.work@gmail.com"},{"hash":"d544f28a430707feba18e7f8b22f2c1b106577e5","date":"2026-09-10T13:27:53+03:00","message":"(fix) Open header patient search results with Enter (#2729)","refs":"","body":"* fix: open header search results with Enter\n\nSelect the focused patient from the displayed search or recently viewed\nlist instead of expecting an array from the keyboard hook. Align the\ncallback type with the hook and preserve advanced-page form submission.\n\n* Reset stale header search selection\n\nClear the keyboard index when the query changes or the focused patient\nis replaced. Preserve it when background refreshes or appended pages keep\nthe same patient at that index. Cover the transitions with rendered tests.","authorName":"Dennis Kigen","authorEmail":"kigen.work@gmail.com"},{"hash":"fcb7a36a901fe4e7072a88dd88e6b6dd1ea72627","date":"2026-09-08T19:51:50+03:00","message":"(fix) Preserve patient search results when clearing attribute filters (#2728)","refs":"","body":"Normalize cleared concept and location selections to an empty string so\nthey are no longer treated as active filters. Cover clearing and applying\nboth field types with regression tests, including missing attributes.","authorName":"Dennis Kigen","authorEmail":"kigen.work@gmail.com"},{"hash":"aa2f12e1960da9ef145339b63478c59ab1df5afe","date":"2026-09-04T16:28:00+03:00","message":"(fix) Pluralise the refine search filter counts and label the forms (#2719)","refs":"","body":"* (fix) Pluralise the refine search filter counts and label the forms\n\nThe Apply button read \"1 filters applied\" because the singular form in en.json carried the plural text. The tablet banner built its sentence from a count in one element and \"search queries added\" in another, which read \"1 search queries added\" and gave translators no way to reorder or pluralise it. The banner now renders one translatable sentence with proper plural forms, keeping the count badge.\n\nThe refine search forms declared role=\"refine-search\" and role=\"refine-search-tablet\", which are not ARIA roles and hide the form semantics assistive technology would otherwise announce. Each form is now labelled by its own heading instead, so it is announced as the \"Refine search\" form.\n\n* Use generated ids for the refine search form labels and keep mock interpolation literal\n\nThe form labels used fixed element ids, which collide when two refine search forms are mounted at once, as they are on the tablet search page today. React's useId gives each instance its own id.\n\nThe test mock's interpolation passed the value straight to String.replace, which would interpret dollar-sign sequences in a value as replacement tokens. A callback keeps the value literal.","authorName":"Dennis Kigen","authorEmail":"kigen.work@gmail.com"},{"hash":"4d8121f988869a859c12afada7ca29039a924486","date":"2026-09-04T14:22:21+03:00","message":"(fix) Apply the configured age bounds to the refine search age field (#2720)","refs":"","body":"* (fix) Apply the configured age bounds to the refine search age field\n\nThe config schema has offered `searchFilterFields.age.min` and `max` since the person attribute filters landed, and the age field reads them, but neither field builder ever passed them through: the built-in fields were created with only a name and a type. Setting the values did nothing. Both the desktop panel and the tablet dialog now hand the configured bounds to the field.\n\nA maximum of 0, the schema default, means no maximum. Carbon marks any value above `max` invalid, so passing 0 through would have flagged every age.\n\n* Explain an out-of-range age\n\nCarbon only draws the invalid border and icon for a value outside min and max. Without invalidText the user gets no reason, so the field now says which range the configured bounds allow.\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Nethmi Rodrigo <nethmi@openmrs.org>","authorName":"Dennis Kigen","authorEmail":"kigen.work@gmail.com"},{"hash":"d4d67713e8b9228e90210e122b1054de4f822bd3","date":"2026-09-04T14:20:28+03:00","message":"(fix) O3-5917: Keep newly added relationship rows correctly associated (#2721)","refs":"","body":"New relationship rows have no server uuid, so every new row rendered with the same undefined React key and React reconciled them by position. The relationship type select was also uncontrolled (defaultValue). After removing one of two new rows, the surviving row kept showing the removed row's person and type while Formik held the other row's values.\n\nGive each new relationship a client-side id when it is pushed, key rows on the server uuid or that id, and drive the select from its Formik value. The id is never sent to the server: saveRelationships only picks the fields it needs.\n\nThe section test's fetchPerson mock returned a response object where the real function returns an array, so no test could exercise the person search. Fix the mock, add an interaction test that fills two rows, removes the first, and checks the second, and fail any test in the file that logs a React key warning.","authorName":"Dennis Kigen","authorEmail":"kigen.work@gmail.com"},{"hash":"cca993b14d3d33cea16a18112dcb4179e1632971","date":"2026-09-04T14:11:29+03:00","message":"(fix) Stop the header search icon opening a second overlay on the tablet search page (#2723)","refs":"","body":"* (fix) Stop the header search icon opening a second overlay on the tablet search page\n\nOn tablet, the search page renders the patient search overlay itself. The header search icon also forces its own overlay open whenever the route is the search page, so the page mounted two complete overlays stacked at the same position: two result lists, two search inputs and two refine forms, each with its own state. The one on top was the page's, so the icon's copy did nothing but duplicate every request and render.\n\nThe icon now only opens its input on the search page in desktop layouts, and renders nothing at all on that page in tablet layouts, where the page's overlay already carries the search input and its own back button. What users see is unchanged.\n\n* Keep the icon's overlay on the phone search page\n\nThe page only renders its own overlay in the tablet layout, so suppressing the icon for every non-desktop layout left phone users on the search page with no search input at all. The icon now steps aside only where the page renders an overlay.\n\n* (test) Clean up patient search icon test setup\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Nethmi Rodrigo <nethmi@openmrs.org>","authorName":"Dennis Kigen","authorEmail":"kigen.work@gmail.com"},{"hash":"5aa90304637d46e0536cf8e6343c2aed296f30a2","date":"2026-09-03T23:53:04+03:00","message":"(fix) Keep the header search input in step with the query in the URL (#2718)","refs":"","body":"On the search page the header search input is seeded from the query in the URL, but only once, when it mounts. A browser back or forward, or a link to another query, changed the results and the heading while the input kept showing the previous term. The compact search and the search bar now follow the term they are given whenever it changes.","authorName":"Dennis Kigen","authorEmail":"kigen.work@gmail.com"},{"hash":"b560585f10a4d207b7d7bdb204857711eb24ad41","date":"2026-09-03T23:30:55+03:00","message":"(test) Assert the search paging tests through what the user sees (#2716)","refs":"","body":"The paging tests stubbed the result views and asserted on attributes of the stubs: which uuid slice was handed to PatientSearchResults, and test ids for the empty and error states. The framework mock stubs the banner's internals, so a real banner cannot show a patient's name in tests. The results stub now renders each patient's name instead, and the empty and error states are the real components, so the assertions read the names and messages a user would see.\n\nThe 1700-result test proves the last page is reachable the way a user would: filter by a postcode only the last patient has and expect that patient to be shown. The error test asserts that no request follows the error state, instead of comparing start indexes against a copy of the component's wave size. The wave test bounds concurrency between one page and the whole set rather than mirroring that constant.\n\nThe file runs under jsdom because the refine-search form submit does not fire under happy-dom, matching advanced-patient-search.test.tsx.","authorName":"Dennis Kigen","authorEmail":"kigen.work@gmail.com"},{"hash":"db742933dbb69eca1f422b45e4b99c82df886a32","date":"2026-09-03T23:22:37+03:00","message":"(fix) Match the birthdate filters against the stored date and trim the postcode filter (#2717)","refs":"","body":"The refine search date of birth filters parsed each patient's birthdate with `new Date` and read the local day, month and year. The backend serialises birthdates as midnight in its own timezone, so in a browser west of that timezone every patient shifted to the previous day and missed the filters, and a patient with no recorded birthdate became 1 January 1970 and matched filters for that date. The filters now read the calendar date off the string, and a patient without a birthdate matches no date of birth filter.\n\nThe postcode filter compared the typed value exactly, so a stray leading or trailing space matched nothing. It is trimmed when the filters are applied, which also keeps the applied-filter count honest for a whitespace-only value.","authorName":"Dennis Kigen","authorEmail":"kigen.work@gmail.com"},{"hash":"5d48e9e791aec4b8fce00334c974ebbee2fb8a9a","date":"2026-09-03T12:54:32+03:00","message":"(fix) Keep patient search on the selected page and load result pages in parallel (#2708)","refs":"","body":"","authorName":"Pius Rubangakene","authorEmail":"piruville@gmail.com"},{"hash":"4708bdfce312569c1b5939cc61b21d23ae7f1052","date":"2026-08-28T17:54:27-04:00","message":"(fix) Add memoization of search results and reduce secondary queries (#2702)","refs":"","body":"","authorName":"Ian","authorEmail":"52504170+ibacher@users.noreply.github.com"},{"hash":"7a2ccf502f6f557aa2628dee2371b2e70f8be5e3","date":"2026-08-27T18:52:46+08:00","message":"(feat) O3-5760: Rework Service Queues dashboard to match design (#2615)","refs":"","body":"* (feat) O3-5760: Rework Service Queues dashboard to match design\n\n* (fix) e2e tests\n\n* (fix) Address review feedback on queues dashboard rework\n\n* (fix) Address review on queues dashboard rework\n\n* (fix) Address review feedback on queues dashboard rework\n\n- Bound the average wait time to entries started today and render '--'\n  instead of 'NaN mins' when the backend has no completed waits to average\n- Surface loading and error states in the Attending section so a failed\n  request is no longer indistinguishable from nobody being attended\n- Cap the Attending cards at three behind a 'View all' toggle and say\n  'No one is being attended' explicitly when the list is empty\n- Exclude Cancelled/Completed/Missed appointments from the expected\n  appointments count and tab\n- Translate appointment statuses, use a single interpolated key for the\n  waiting list tab label, and use the framework age() helper so infants\n  no longer render as '0 years old'\n\n* (fix) O3-5760: Address second round of review feedback on queues dashboard\n\nAdds concepts.waitingStatusConceptUuid so the waiting list, its tab count and\nthe \"Waiting\" metric stop overloading defaultStatusConceptUuid, which only\ndescribes the status a newly created queue entry starts in. All three read the\nnew config, so the count cannot disagree with the rows beneath it.\n\n- Count the waiting list via queue-entry-metrics instead of paging through\n  every entry. useQueueEntriesMetrics now reports isLoading and error so the\n  tab label shows no momentary \"(0)\" before the request settles.\n- Drop useServiceMetricsCount: it hardcoded status=Waiting as a concept name\n  and has no remaining callers.\n- Send forDate as an ISO 8601 string. The appointments module's DateUtil does\n  not parse a ZZ numeric offset. The test now asserts the value, not the path.\n- Show the selected service in the header even when the location is \"All\",\n  since the modal permits that combination, and reset the service when the\n  default location resolves, as services are scoped to a location.\n- Look the expected-appointments name cell up through an id/patientUuid map\n  rather than scanning every row on each render.\n- Guard the service sort against a missing display, order attending-patients\n  imports components before hooks, and drop an unused @carbon/type import.\n\n* (fix) O3-5760: Trim the waitingStatusConceptUuid description\n\nIts contrast with defaultStatusConceptUuid belongs in review, not in the\nconfig reference that implementers read.\n\n* (fix) O3-5760: Scope the wait-time metric and Call action to the waiting status\n\n* (fix) O3-5760: Remove the appointments features from the dashboard\n\nThe Expected appointments tab and Appointments today card only match\nappointments whose location equals the selected queue location exactly,\nand the alternative leaks other locations' appointments. Dropping both\nuntil location tagging is settled.\n\nAlso formats Avg. wait time like the Wait time column, and shows --\nwhen the backend has nothing to average.\n\n* (fix) O3-5760: Round the average wait time before guarding on it\n\n* (fix) O3-5760: Send the wait-time window as UTC\n\nThe queue module parses startedOnOrAfter with a zone-less\nSimpleDateFormat, so browser-local midnight was read in the server's\ntimezone and hid everything queued before the client's offset elapsed.\n\n* (fix) O3-5760: Restructure the Attending card details\n\n* (fix) O3-5760: Move the service and priority into a card footer\n\nSeparates them from the demographics with a rule, service left and pill\nright, per design review. The card element is now the link itself rather\nthan a wrapper around one.\n\n* (fix) O3-5760: Count the entries a search leaves in the waiting list heading\n\n`totalCount` is the server's count of every waiting entry, so the heading kept\nreporting the full list while the table showed only the search results.\n\n* (fix) O3-5760: Send the metrics window as an unambiguous instant\n\nThe queue module could not parse a timezone offset, so browser-local midnight\nwas being converted to UTC and sent zone-less — correct only because servers\nusually run in UTC. openmrs-module-queue now parses REST date parameters with\nConversionUtil, so send an ISO-8601 instant and let the server resolve it.\n\nRequires queue module 3.1.0 or later.\n\n* (chore) Require queue module 3.1.0 for queue-entry-metrics\n\nThe average wait time card sends `startedOnOrAfter` as an ISO-8601 instant,\nwhich only queue 3.1.0 onwards parses, so declare that in the backend\ndependencies instead of noting it in a code comment. The `-0` prerelease\nfloor keeps SNAPSHOT builds valid for testing.\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Ujjawal Prabhat <ujjawal@Ujjawals-MacBook-Pro.local>\nCo-authored-by: jwnasambu <33891016+jwnasambu@users.noreply.github.com>\nCo-authored-by: Nethmi Rodrigo <nethmi@openmrs.org>","authorName":"Ujjawal Prabhat","authorEmail":"UjjawalPrabhat1@gmail.com"},{"hash":"0c695bcda73aa438cf88ba10cdddfe27ab22d590","date":"2026-07-30T14:22:27+08:00","message":"(feat) O3-5761: List checked-in patients before search when adding to queue (#2633)","refs":"","body":"* (feat) O3-5761: List checked-in patients before search when adding to queue\n\n* (feat) O3-5761: Render checked-in patients with the patient banner\n\nReuse the framework patient-banner components for the checked-in patients\nshortlist so its rows match patient-search results, and pass a mapped FHIR\npatient to the selection callback instead of a bare uuid.\n\n- Add mapActiveVisitPatientToFhir to convert the REST visit patient into the\n  minimal FHIR shape the banner components expect\n- Widen the useActiveVisits custom representation accordingly and fetch all\n  pages via useOpenmrsFetchAll so the list isn't truncated\n- Drop the restrictToToday parameter; the server-side fromStartDate filter\n  already scopes results to today\n- Move the config gate to AddPatientToQueueButton and rename the property to\n  showCheckedInPatientsBeforeSearch\n- Add loading and error states, and cover the new behaviour with tests\n\n* (chore) O3-5761: Clarify that the checked-in patients list is location-scoped\n\nThe queue-entry exclusion is filtered by the selected queue location, but the\ndoc comment and empty-state copy implied it covered any queue. Reword both to\nmatch the actual scope.\n\n* (chore) O3-5761: Pin the location scope of the checked-in patients exclusion\n\nThe shortlist filters active visits against queue entries scoped to the selected location, which is deliberate: a patient can legitimately hold entries at several locations, and the backend only rejects a repeat entry in the same queue. Nothing asserted the criteria passed to useQueueEntries, so that scope could have drifted silently.\n\n* (chore) translation changes\n\n* (chore) O3-5761: Clarify that the checked-in patients shortlist is today-only\n\nThe docblock said the list shows patients \"with an active visit\", but\nuseActiveVisits always sends fromStartDate=<today>, so an open visit that\nstarted before today is excluded. Spell out the today-only scope.\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: NethmiRodrigo <nethmi.dilinika@gmail.com>\nCo-authored-by: Ujjawal Prabhat <ujjawal@10-64-49-196.0200.binb.id.iosda.org>\nCo-authored-by: Nethmi Rodrigo <nethmi@openmrs.org>","authorName":"Ujjawal Prabhat","authorEmail":"UjjawalPrabhat1@gmail.com"},{"hash":"595e97286e45a540a4ddf72dbda646a3c01e78dc","date":"2026-07-27T16:42:07+03:00","message":"(feat) Improve no active visit empty state in admission workspace (#2172)","refs":"","body":"* feat: improve no active visit admission state\n\nShow a start visit prompt when a patient without an active visit is selected for admission.\n\nAdd scoped workspace styles and test coverage for the no active visit admission workflow.\n\n* Show admit and start visit buttons on ward admission patient search cards\n\nImplements the design agreed in the PR review discussion: in the Add\npatient to ward search, the patient card is no longer clickable. Patients\nwith an active visit get an enabled Admit button that opens the admission\nworkspace. Patients without one get a start visit button next to a\ndisabled Admit button, which enables in place once the visit is saved.\n\nThe patient search workspace gains an optional selectPatientButton prop\nso the ward can configure the button without leaking it into the other\nconsumers of the search workspace (appointments, patient lists, queues).\n\n* Pass the patient to the start visit button slot on search result cards\n\nThe banner rendered start-visit-button-slot2 without the patient in the\nslot state, so the start visit button launched the visit form with an\nundefined patient prop. The visit form and the extensions it hosts, like\nthe billing check-in form, dereference that patient, which surfaced as\nrequests to patient/undefined and post-save callback failures on billing\nenabled instances.\n\n* Give the admit patient workspace a footer and visit context\n\nThe workspace rendered its primary action as a ghost link floating in an\notherwise empty panel, with a back link of equal visual weight beneath it\nand no information beyond the patient banner. The admit and back actions\nnow sit in the standard workspace footer button bar, matching the bed\nselection form, and the body shows the active visit's type, location,\nand start time alongside the existing admission warnings.\n\nAdmitPatientButton accepts optional kind and size props so the footer can\nrender it as a primary action without changing its ghost styling in the\nadmission requests bench.\n\n* Auto-open the admission workspace after starting a visit\n\nAfter the visit form saves in the Add patient to ward flow, the admission\nworkspace now opens automatically for the same patient instead of\nreturning the user to the search results to click Admit. The callback\nflows from the ward's workspace props through the patient search context\nand banner into the visit form's onVisitStarted hook.\n\nLaunching a child workspace immediately after another closes previously\ntripped a lifecycle race in workspace2 that could mount the closed form's\ncomponent with the new workspace's props. That race was fixed in\nopenmrs/openmrs-esm-core#1807, which is included in the framework build\nthis branch resolves after rebasing onto main. Verified locally against\nthat build: repeated start-visit-then-admit flows land on the admission\nworkspace with no stale component mount and no patient/undefined\nrequests.\n\n* Use flex instead of hard-coded button widths in admission workspace footer\n\nCarbon's .cds--btn-set .cds--btn rule caps footer buttons at 196px and\nout-specifies a single CSS module class, which is why the previous rule\nneeded !important. Doubling the class wins on specificity instead, and\nflex: 1 splits the row evenly without hard-coding a 50% width. With two\nbuttons the layout is unchanged; in the error state the lone back button\nnow fills the footer instead of stopping at half width.\n\nAddresses review feedback from @ibacher.","authorName":"Dennis Kigen","authorEmail":"kigen.work@gmail.com"},{"hash":"e4aacbd5a6242821c4f956230535f598cdeac835","date":"2026-07-24T19:54:04-04:00","message":"(fix) Patient search should bypass service worker caching (#2638)","refs":"","body":"","authorName":"Ian","authorEmail":"52504170+ibacher@users.noreply.github.com"},{"hash":"39be6d5abb7182bd5b3e08b8684aefb6e046542f","date":"2026-06-01T17:40:34-04:00","message":"(feat) O3-5714: Improve performance with multi-paged patient search results (#2554)","refs":"","body":"* O3-5714: Improve performance with multi-paged patient search results\n\nSeveral notable fixes for the compact-patient-search component:\n\n* Previously, each call to `useSWRInfinite()` was, in essence, returning\n  new copies of existing data, which lead to unnecessary re-renders. This\n  has been fixed by setting `keepPreviousData` to `true`\n* Previously, when `useSWRInfinite()` set `isLoading` to `true`, all\n  results were replaced with placeholder. Since this gets set to `true`\n  even when, e.g., loading a second page of results, this resulted in\n  unnecessary unmounts and recreations, which was both a memory leak and\n  lead to a stampede of requests.\n* All search results were previously rendered and retained. This leads\n  to stampedes of secondary queries (e.g., for patient photos, queue\n  status, visit status, etc.). Instead, this PR moves us to using list\n  virtualization so that roughly 10-18 items are retained in a React\n  query. Large scrolls backwards or forwards have some slight glitches\n  as components are re-rendered, but the easiest way to fix this is in\n  the components rendering the secondary queries themselves.\n* Recent patients, however, are not virtualized at all, as we rely on\n  this being a limited list that is safe to load.\n* A mistake in the call to `useArrowNavigation()` resulted in the arrow\n  keys only being usable for up to the number of `recentPatients`\n* This PR adds additional component-level memoization where it makes\n  sense to speed up rendering. In addition, in the context of search\n  results, we re-tune SWR to more aggressively cache so that there's\n  less need to re-try, e.g., patient photo queries\n* Additionally, this PR makes two fixes the service queues banner tag.\n  First, if it is rendered outside the patient chart, a wrapper component\n  is used so no query needs to be issued. Second, the query that was\n  used overfetched data, especially as the queue details in the modal\n  are basically reloaded, so the representation has been updated to\n  minimize the data requested. This is one of the biggest contributing\n  components.\n\n* Fixes from code review\n\n* Address Copilot comment","authorName":"Ian","authorEmail":"52504170+ibacher@users.noreply.github.com"},{"hash":"eb42a62c491f87c2914681e5253b5c2e1af9144f","date":"2026-04-28T11:22:13+05:30","message":"(fix) O3-5634: Type safe patient search app (#2512)","refs":"","body":"","authorName":"Dilan Kavishka","authorEmail":"109354298+dilankavishka@users.noreply.github.com"},{"hash":"fb6d9a2a40f7b9b6e9c9f48ab99e5bc734c8fb49","date":"2026-03-27T17:25:47+03:00","message":"(fix) Improve patient search robustness and accessibility (#2404)","refs":"","body":"","authorName":"Dennis Kigen","authorEmail":"kigen.work@gmail.com"},{"hash":"bc06adf7eb92305b3f13849c196acb2a1869dff6","date":"2026-03-26T22:11:07+03:00","message":"(fix) Hide generic overflow actions in task-specific patient search pickers (#2409)","refs":"","body":"","authorName":"Dennis Kigen","authorEmail":"kigen.work@gmail.com"},{"hash":"219529a47911448f4f1fb357475102eddc5ed262","date":"2026-02-26T15:15:59+03:00","message":"(fix) Filter voided patients from recently viewed list (#2284)","refs":"","body":"The REST API returns voided patients when fetched by UUID (unlike the\nsearch endpoint, which excludes them server-side). This means voided\npatient UUIDs persisted in the user's patientsVisited property would\nstill render in the recently viewed list.\n\nAdd `voided` to the custom representation and filter voided patients\nin useRestPatients.","authorName":"Dennis Kigen","authorEmail":"kigen.work@gmail.com"},{"hash":"240d4728294a690aaf957f12320fed287bd4c6b7","date":"2026-01-26T12:04:18+03:00","message":"(feat) O3-5342: Add ability to search queue services  (#2192)","refs":"","body":"","authorName":"Laurent Ouma","authorEmail":"98098891+Omoshlawi@users.noreply.github.com"},{"hash":"2fe547d1f48f1d4c02db97737bd520831c6783f0","date":"2026-01-23T20:49:44+03:00","message":"(fix) Improve recently viewed patients feature behavior (#2221)","refs":"","body":"The recently viewed patients feature had several issues that could confuse\nusers and cause unnecessary network requests:\n\n1. When a user had no viewing history, the component rendered nothing instead\nof showing an empty state, leaving blank space in the UI.\n\n2. The showRecentlySearchedPatients config flag only controlled whether the UI\nwas displayed, but tracking (POST requests) and preloading still occurred even\nwhen disabled.\n\n3. Users could briefly see \"No recently viewed patients\" before their actual\nhistory loaded, due to a race condition between fetching user properties and\nrendering the empty state.\n\nThis commit:\n\n- Fixes blank UI when user has no recently viewed patients by adding fallback\nempty state for null data\n- Respects the feature flag for tracking and preload, not just UI display\n- Prevents premature empty state flash while user properties are loading\n- Updates empty state copy to \"No recently viewed patients\"\n- Uses custom:(userProperties) representation to preserve other properties on update\n\nThe feature now fails gracefully, fully respects its config flag, and shows accurate\nloading states.","authorName":"Dennis Kigen","authorEmail":"kigen.work@gmail.com"}],"totalCount":34}"}],"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_01XnYuZhMQF5Vqxjn4PcVcqY","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"rule"}}]}
